    Summary: "Asks the host whether the bee at `url` is still the one we cached, without\n downloading it. Pass the cached tag as `cachedVersionTag` to send a\n conditional request: a compliant host answers 304 and the result reports\n BasisRemoteValidator.NotModified, which is the cheapest possible answer.\n\n \n\nHosts that ignore conditional headers (Google Drive serves `Last-Modified` but\n does not honour `If-Modified-Since`) still return their validators on the normal\n response, so the caller can compare tags itself. Hosts that publish neither return a result\n with no value, which callers must treat as \"cannot tell\" rather than \"unchanged\"."
