  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: MatrixFor
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - limb
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Replaces each limb's radius with one measured from the avatar's own skinned meshes.\n\n The body plan is proportions: a radius is a fraction of hips-to-head, so every avatar of the same\n height gets the same limbs however differently they are actually built. This measures instead - every\n sampled vertex is given to the limb segment it sits nearest, and the limb takes a percentile of those\n distances. A heavy boot gets a thicker foot and a thin wrist gets a thinner forearm, on the avatar\n that is standing there rather than on an average of all of them.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F Silently does nothing when the meshes cannot be read, which is the common case for uploaded\n avatars - Read/Write is off by default and the ray scene already treats unreadable geometry as\n ordinary (see BasisGlobalIlluminationRayScene). Falling back to the plan is the point: this improves\n the fit where it can and is never required for correctness.\n\n Runs once, at resolve, and is bounded by FitVertexBudget - a hundred thousand vertex\n avatar is sampled by stride rather than read whole."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
