  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: CapsuleSides
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The one mesh every limb of every avatar is an instance of. Built once, never written again, so the\n acceleration structure holds a single small BLAS for every body in the room and never rebuilds it.\n\n Authored as a unit: radius 1, ends at y = +/-1, so MatrixFor is a pure TRS. Eight\n sides and two hemisphere rings is about 150 triangles - the silhouette is what carries occlusion,\n and a rounder capsule would move the result by less than one texel of a half resolution gather.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F The +/-1 above is load bearing and this mesh used to break it. Both matrix builders scale Y by\n the limb's HALF length, which places the ends on the two bones only if the mesh ends at +/-1. It was\n authored as a full sphere sitting on each end of a unit cylinder, so it ended at +/-2 - and every\n capsule in the room came out exactly TWICE the length of the bone it stood for, reaching a whole half\n limb past each joint. A shin capsule ran from above the knee to twenty centimetres under the floor, a\n thigh capsule up into the pelvis, and the legs of every avatar sat inside a solid overlapping column\n of them. That is what the black patches around people's legs were: surfaces enclosed by their own\n proxy, in both the ray traced gather and ambient occlusion.\n\n So the cap is a fraction of the half length rather than equal to it. The body stays a cylinder to\n within CapFraction of each end and the tip rounds off exactly ON the bone. Adjacent\n limbs share a joint, so keeping the cap short is what stops a lens shaped hole opening at every knee\n and elbow where two tapers meet."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
