    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Classifies the GPU the player is really rendering on, which the build target cannot answer.\n A Windows build launched from a Steam Frame library runs x86 under Proton on an Adreno\n reached through Turnip, and a Snapdragon Windows-on-ARM laptop is the same shape: every\n rendering cost is a mobile cost while Application.isMobilePlatform is false.\n Anything that wants to spend by hardware class rather than by build target asks here.\n\n \n\nSystemInfo is main-thread only, so the probe is primed from device\n management startup and every later read, on any thread, hits the cache. A read that beats\n the priming from another thread answers desktop and leaves the probe unrun, so the next\n main-thread read still gets the real hardware rather than a cached guess."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
