  - TypeFullName: BasisSceneScan
    MemberName: BasisSceneScan
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "One shared answer to \"what is in the scene\", so that the several systems which have to discover\n their own content by type do not each pay for the discovery.\n\n `FindObjectsByType` walks every loaded object of a type and allocates twice - once natively and\n once more through `Resources.ConvertObjects` to hand back a typed array - so it is the sort of\n call that should happen once for the frame and be read by everybody, not once per interested party.\n Global illumination and ray traced ambient occlusion want exactly the same two sets (every renderer,\n every animator) on exactly the same cadence, and before this they each took their own copy: five\n full-scene walks per rescan window where three would do.\n\n The cache is aged rather than framed on purpose. Tying it to the frame would only dedupe consumers\n that happen to scan on the SAME frame, which would force them into lockstep - the opposite of what is\n wanted, since spreading the scans across different frames is what keeps any one frame cheap. An age\n lets a consumer say \"anything from the last two seconds will do\", so whoever asks first pays and\n everyone asking later in the window reads the same array for nothing, whatever frame they are on.\n\n The arrays are shared and must be treated as read only. They also hold references for as long as they\n are cached, so an entry may be a destroyed object by the time it is read: every consumer already null\n checks, because that was equally true of a freshly taken array the moment anything was destroyed."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
