  - TypeFullName: BasisTracedCategory
    MemberName: BasisTracedCategory
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Which half of the room one instance in a ray tracing acceleration structure belongs to.\n\n Ambient occlusion and global illumination trace the same avatars and the same world, and each has its\n own idea of which of the two it wants - the panel offers Avatars, World, or both to each effect\n separately. Tagging the instance and masking at trace time is what lets ONE structure answer both\n questions: the structure holds the union of what the two asked for, and each trace walks only its own\n half of it.\n\n Without this the only way to give the two effects different content is a structure each, which is what\n the frame paid for before: two scans of the scene, two transform sweeps and two full builds every\n frame, over the same geometry, with every avatar's capsules registered twice.\n\n Lives in Common because both effects name it and neither should have to depend on the other."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
