  - TypeFullName: BasisTracedCategory
    MemberName: AvatarProxy
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The capsules that stand in for a body, as opposed to geometry anybody drew.\n\n Its own bit because a proxy is the one thing in the structure that does NOT match what is on screen.\n Rays start from the depth buffer - the avatar's real rendered surface - and a surface sitting inside\n its own capsule fires every ray into the inside of it and reads as fully enclosed. Global illumination\n recognises that case by reading a flag off the instance it hit; ambient occlusion has no instance\n buffer to read, so it separates the two by MASK instead and traces the capsules on their own. Inside\n a proxy-only trace every hit is a proxy by construction, which is what lets the same back-face test\n work there without an instance to check it against."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
