  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: StoreData
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - intervalSeconds
    - rotation
    - position
    - muscles
    - null
    ParamDocs:
    - Time since previous frame, in seconds.
    - Root rotation.
    - Root position.
    - Humanoid muscle values (length 95 expected).
    - Avatar scale.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Writes one frame to disk.\n Layout (per frame, in this exact order):\n   float IntervalSeconds\n   Quaternion rotation (x, y, z, w)\n   Vector3 position (x, y, z)\n   float muscles[95]\n   float scale\n\n Total: 104 floats = 416 bytes.\n\n The frame is packed on the caller's thread into a pooled buffer and written by\n a dedicated writer thread, so the per-frame capture path never touches the\n FileStream. Byte layout is identical to the old BinaryWriter output\n (little-endian floats)."
