  - TypeFullName: CutoutCoveragePass
    MemberName: CutoutCoveragePass
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: ScriptableRenderPass
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "With post-processing off and both textures overridden Off, a multisampled target is the only\n thing keeping URP's intermediate colour/depth attachments alive for this camera. Antialiasing\n Off (and the always-single-sampled secondary viewer textures) drops it to rendering straight\n into the shared reflection texture, which comes back holding nothing but URP's background\n clear. Asking for the depth texture restores the attachments \u2014 the same graph the mirror runs\n at every MSAA level \u2014 for one depth copy on the renders that would otherwise be empty."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
