  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Audio.BasisVoiceLevel
    MemberName: BasisVoiceLevel
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Turns a voice signal's RMS into the 0..1 loudness that avatars and UI animate against,\n so the microphone meter, a remote speaker's avatar and anything an avatar author binds\n all read the same scale.\n \n\nThe mapping is the one `BasisLocalVolumeMeterUI` already draws with: RMS to\n dBFS, then MinDb..MaxDb remapped onto 0..1. Linear amplitude\n is the wrong scale to hand an avatar \u2014 the AGC lands speech near 0.1 RMS, so a linear\n parameter would spend a whole conversation between 0.05 and 0.2.\n\n\n\nLevels are always measured BEFORE the listener's attenuation \u2014 distance, per-player\n volume, the directivity cone \u2014 so anything driven by them reads the same to everyone in\n the room rather than dimming as you walk away, or sitting at 0 for whoever turned the\n speaker down."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
