  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisAnnouncedTrackerRoles
    MemberName: BasisAnnouncedTrackerRoles
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bypasses the manual tracker calibration for trackers that already announce their body part.\n The generic convention is built in: SteamVR encodes any tracker's user-assigned role,\n whatever the brand, in its controller type (\"vive_tracker_waist\", ...; TrustSteamVRRoles,\n default off since most setups leave those roles unset or stale). Integration packages\n register more specific announcement conventions via RegisterSource (e.g. the\n SlimeVR package's \"human://WAIST\"-style serials); sources run first and can also suppress\n a device from the generic path. When such trackers appear this forces the matching Basis\n role through a runtime tracker-role override and runs the standard FullBodyCalibration\n pass once the set has settled \u2014 the classifier binds the forced roles without scoring\n while the pass still captures the tracker-to-bone offsets, per-effector rotation\n calibration and bend hints, exactly like a menu-triggered calibration. Trackers announcing\n nothing keep going through the normal geometric classification in the same pass."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
