    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Overrides a remote install's spawn pose with that player's latest network pose.\n\n Every remote call site passes Vector3.zero because\n BasisRemoteAvatarDriver.RemoteCalibration snaps root and hips onto the\n network pose right after the install. That snap is too late for anything that seeds\n itself from world position during Instantiate: Awake/OnEnable run INSIDE the\n Instantiate call, so jiggle trees, colliders and constraints all come up believing the\n avatar lives at the world origin, and only a teleport-by-delta afterwards rescues them.\n Spawning at the right place removes the need for the rescue.\n\n Hips world is the closest pose available here \u2014 the root derivation calibration uses\n needs References/TPose, which are not read until the avatar exists. The remaining\n hips-vs-root offset is under a metre and calibration corrects it in the same frame.\n No-ops for the local player (parented under the player root, already in place) and for\n a remote with no receiver yet."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
