  - TypeFullName: BasisAvatarModelCache+BoneDecodeOperatorData
    MemberName: BoneDecodeOperatorData
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The folded generic->rig decode operators for every wire slot, indexed by slot in\n BasisBoneRotationCompression.BONE_WRITE_ORDER (NOT by HumanBodyBones)."
    Remarks: "Safe to key on the Avatar asset because every input is: the rest tables come from\n TposeLocal/TposeFromRoot, the character basis comes from the\n same capture, and which slots resolve a bone is fixed by the rig. The per-instance half of\n the same loop \u2014 the bone Transforms \u2014 stays per player.\n \n\nThe arrays double as the snapshot `RemoteBoneJobSystem.AddRemotePlayer` defers\n with. It used to `ToArray()` the receiver's two NativeArrays because those are owned\n by the receiver and can be disposed under a recalibration before the add commits; a\n cache-owned immutable array has no such lifetime problem, so the copy goes away."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
