  - TypeFullName: BasisAvatarModelCache+TposeHierarchyData
    MemberName: TposeHierarchyData
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The local position/rotation every transform under the animator root holds once the T-pose\n controller has been applied and evaluated, in `GetComponentsInChildren` order."
    Remarks: "Posing an avatar into its T-pose costs two `runtimeAnimatorController` assignments (an\n animator rebind each) plus a full humanoid `Animator.Update` \u2014 the same pair\n `BasisRemoteAvatarDriver` already skips for far LOD avatars, and the dominant cost of\n installing the loading dummy inline on the transmit tick when a player leaves avatar range.\n The result is a property of the model, not the instance: the same prefab instantiated again\n starts from the same authored locals and the same clip drives it to the same pose. Recording\n it once lets every later install of that model write the locals back directly.\n \n\nIndex 0 is the animator root itself and is never replayed \u2014 its local transform is the\n instance's placement under `AvatarParent`, not a bone pose."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
