    Summary: Native buffers detached from evicted entries, freed only at Clear.
    Remarks: "\u26A0\uFE0F Freeing here is a crash, and it was one: every grid that restored from this entry holds a\n non-owning VIEW of HandPoseGridData.SharedCells, and a NativeArray view has no\n way to observe its owner being disposed \u2014 `IsCreated` keeps returning true, so\n `ExpandFingerChannels`' guard passes and the read throws ObjectDisposedException.\n\n Worse, eviction reaches here from `BasisAvatarFactory.DeleteLastAvatar`, which is\n async void: its continuation runs on the Unity synchronization context and can land between\n `BeginNetworkCompute` and `JoinPendingCompute` \u2014 with the parallel finger\n expansion mid-flight over these exact cells. There is no lock to take and no refcount to\n consult, so the buffer simply outlives the entry.\n\n Retaining is not a regression: before the cells were shared, every player allocated their\n own copy and nothing ever freed those either. This holds ONE per model instead of one per\n player, and the eviction still does the half that matters for correctness \u2014 the entry stops\n being handed out, so a destroyed asset (or a reused entity id) can never serve stale data."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
