  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: DetermineAction
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - connector
    - lastInfo
    - null
    ParamDocs:
    - The bundle metadata for the loaded avatar.
    - "The player's cached PerformanceInfo\n from the last load \u2014 what was actually trimmed on disk."
    - "When set, nothing Evaluate checks can\n block this player; trim categories are still reconciled."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Decide what the settings bridge should do with a player after a limit\n change. Compares each category's currently-kept count (derived from\n metadata + stored trim counts) against what the new limits would keep\n and picks the cheapest correct response:\n\n   \u2022 ReconcileAction.None \u2014 no category would change and\n     the hard-block flag didn't flip. Skip the player entirely.\n   \u2022 ReconcileAction.TrimInPlace \u2014 every change tightens\n     an existing count. Destroy the extras on the live avatar; no reload,\n     no bundle I/O, no setup pass.\n   \u2022 ReconcileAction.Reload \u2014 a trim category relaxed\n     (destroyed components need to come back), the limit got disabled,\n     or the hard-block flag flipped. Full `ReloadAvatar` required."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
