  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisIgnoredCalibrationTrackers
    MemberName: BasisIgnoredCalibrationTrackers
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Devices kept out of full-body calibration, recognized by the identity strings their runtime\n reports. Hand-tracking bridges publish their solved hands as ordinary SteamVR trackers carrying\n no role, so the geometric classifier sees two extra free trackers sitting at hand height and\n binds them to LowerArm/Shoulder \u2014 dragging those roles off the real trackers. They are not\n body-segment trackers, so they are dropped from the constellation rather than scored against it.\n\n Gated behind IgnoreHandTrackingDevices (Tracker Settings, off by default): the only evidence\n here is a device name, so an unconditional list would silently stop a legitimately-named\n tracker from ever calibrating."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
