  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    MemberName: BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Watches the instance population and, once per app run for each population tier, offers to\n switch BasisPerformanceMode on at the level that tier warrants. Pumped from\n the central tick; no MonoBehaviour.\n\n Each tier asks at most once per app lifetime \u2014 the static \"asked\" flags reset on restart,\n so the offer comes back the next time the app is launched into a crowded instance. Crossing\n a higher tier supersedes the lower ones (their flags are marked asked at the same time), so\n joining an already-huge instance shows a single prompt instead of stacking several.\n\n The dialogue lists the values the level will actually resolve to, read back from the mode\n itself, so the text can never drift from the effect. Nothing here is asked when the player\n has already turned the mode on to at least that level, or has it following the population\n automatically.\n\n Accepting arms the level through BasisPerformanceMode.SetLevelFromPopulation,\n which tags it as crowd-driven so BasisPerformanceMode.Simulate relaxes it back\n down on its own \u2014 no second prompt \u2014 once the population that justified it thins out again,\n whether that's this instance emptying or the player leaving to a smaller one. A level picked\n by hand from the Graphics tab is never touched this way."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
