  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisMenuPromptRestore
    MemberName: BasisMenuPromptRestore
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Unsolicited prompts (incoming direct connections, moderation notices, world load\n requests, the crowd and eye-tracking suggestions) force the main menu open so they\n are actually seen. Forcing it open rebuilds the menu from scratch, and everything\n parented to its PanelRoot goes down with it \u2014 the page the user was on and the\n virtual keyboard they were typing on.\n\n BasisMainMenu.Open snapshots both on the way down; the prompt calls\n RestoreAfterPrompt when its panel closes and they come back, the same\n way Settings is reopened after a reset. The snapshot is bound to the menu instance\n it was taken for, so a release that lands after the menu was closed or rebuilt again\n (Unity defers Destroy to the end of the frame) restores nothing."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
