  - TypeFullName: BasisFingerReconstructionDiagnostics
    MemberName: BasisFingerReconstructionDiagnostics
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Measures how far the local player's live finger bones sit from the pose a receiver would\n reconstruct out of the twenty curl/splay scalars, WITHOUT changing the wire.\n\n This exists to answer one question before the finger block commits to a format: can the grid\n reproduce what is actually on the bones? Every finger backend in the codebase writes only\n BasisFingerPose, and BasisFingerSlerpJob then drives all thirty joints from it, so the answer\n should be \"yes, to float noise\". Anything else is a writer the survey missed, and finding it\n here costs a log line instead of a wire revision.\n\n Two different numbers, and the difference matters:\n\n   Lag       angle(grid at the CURRENT percentages, live bone). Non-zero by design \u2014 the local\n             driver slerps toward the grid target at LerpSpeed, so the bones trail it. This\n             bounds how far a receiver sampling the raw percentages lands from what the sender\n             is looking at; it is a smoothing question, not a representability one.\n\n   Manifold  angle to the BEST-FIT grid pose, searched over every node. This is the real\n             question: is the live pose reachable by some curl/splay at all? Lag cannot make\n             this large; only an off-grid writer can.\n\n Undriven joints are counted separately. RebuildTransformAccess only drives joints whose\n mapping Has flag is set, while the compressor sends every bone it can resolve \u2014 so a joint\n that exists but is not driven carries a real bind/animator rotation the grid never produced,\n and a grid-only format would overwrite it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
