  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Rendering.BasisGraphicsApiManifest
    MemberName: BasisGraphicsApiManifest
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IPreprocessBuildWithReport
    Interfaces:
    - IPostprocessBuildWithReport
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bakes the graphics APIs a build ships into Resources, because nothing reads that list back\n at runtime and BasisGraphicsApiSelection needs it to answer the only question the Renderer\n section rests on: is there more than one renderer to choose between. Without it the runtime\n has to hardcode the list, which goes stale the first time anyone edits Player Settings and\n goes stale silently \u2014 a single-API build would go on offering a second renderer it has no\n compiled shaders for.\n\n Written before the build and removed after it, so the generated file never lands in a commit.\n A build that fails partway can leave it behind; it is one line of text and the next build\n overwrites it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
