  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisInteractTargetPicker
    MemberName: BasisInteractTargetPicker
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Chooses which interactable a hand takes when the pointer ray and the proximity bubble disagree.\n Pure geometry with no scene, player or network dependency so the rules can be tested directly.\n\n Three bands, in order:\n\n \u2022 InHand \u2014 inside the object's own grab radius of the hand bone. Closing your hand on a\n   prop takes it no matter where you are pointing, in any direction.\n\n \u2022 Aimed \u2014 inside a cone about the pointer ray that widens with distance, so aim tolerance\n   stays roughly constant in screen terms rather than collapsing at arm's length. Scored by\n   distance along the ray with off-axis distance as a light tiebreak, matching\n   BasisJiggleGrabPicker.TryScorePointing.\n\n \u2022 Nearby \u2014 within reach but off-aim. Preserves loose bubble grabbing for props beside the\n   hand while keeping them behind anything actually aimed at."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
