  - TypeFullName: BasisFingerSlerpJob
    MemberName: BasisFingerSlerpJob
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IJobParallelForTransform
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Burst-compiled job that bilinearly interpolates each finger joint's target rotation from the baked 2D pose\n grid, slerps the current rotation toward it, and writes the result to transforms via TransformAccessArray.\n Uses JointMapping to recover (fingerIdx, jointIdx) from the compact TAA layout.\n\n The interpolation used to be a separate 10-item job feeding a 30-entry target array. Folding it in costs no\n extra slerps -- that job produced 3 joints per finger and this one already runs per joint, so the same 3\n grid slerps happen either way -- and it removes a job dispatch, a dependency fence and the array round-trip\n from a chain whose total work is ~3 us but whose completion cost an order of magnitude more than that."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
