  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Platform.BasisDesktopClipboard
    MemberName: BasisDesktopClipboard
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The client's clipboard-paste bridge, and the counterpart to BasisDesktopFileDrop:\n that one covers images the user drags in as files, this one covers images the user copies as\n data \u2014 a screenshot tool, \"copy image\" in a browser, a paint program \u2014 where nothing was ever\n written to disk and there is no path to hand anyone.\n\n Unlike the file drop this needs no window subclass. Windows delivers no paste message to a game\n window (WM_PASTE is an edit-control convention), so the chord is read from the input system in\n Dispatch and the clipboard is opened right there on the main thread. That also\n means it works in the editor, where the file drop's WndProc hook cannot run.\n\n Formats are tried richest-first: a real PNG or GIF keeps its alpha and its animation, while\n BasisClipboardImageFormat.Bitmap is the lossy floor that every source offers.\n Copied *files* are forwarded to BasisDesktopFileDrop.SubmitDroppedFiles instead,\n so pasting a file from Explorer behaves exactly like dragging it in."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
