  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Rendering.BasisGpuOcclusionCulling
    MemberName: BasisGpuOcclusionCulling
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Startup switch for URP's GPU occlusion culling \u2014 the GPU Resident Drawer's depth-pyramid\n occlusion test on game cameras.\n\n The drawer snapshots its settings when it is constructed and the per-frame path reads that\n snapshot rather than the pipeline asset, so writing the asset field changes nothing on its\n own; the drawer has to be rebuilt. That rebuild re-registers every MeshRenderer and LODGroup\n in the loaded scenes, which is why this applies once at boot while the scene is still the\n loading scene, and a change made later waits for a restart instead of paying that mid-session."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
