  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Rendering.BasisRTAOCaptureOverride
    MemberName: BasisRTAOCaptureOverride
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A per-photo substitute for the \"look\" half of RTAO's settings - the fields a camera can\n reasonably want different from the player's live settings for one shot. Deliberately excludes\n Quality (a capture already forces Ultra unconditionally - see\n BasisRTAOIntegration.BeginCapture) and Other Cameras (also forced on\n unconditionally, so a photo is never silently missing occlusion because the player turned\n mirror/handheld occlusion off to save frame time).\n\n Mode, ApplyMode, Layers and SkinnedMeshes are stored as the canonical option strings\n BasisRTAOSettingsMap already parses, and DenoisePasses as the plain 0-3 int\n BasisRTAOFeature.DenoisePassesOverride itself wants, rather than the enum/LayerMask\n types - so nothing that only ever assigns into this struct needs to name a\n `Basis.Rendering.RTAO` type, and com.basis.camera never needs an asmdef reference to\n com.basis.rtao to use it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
