  - TypeFullName: BasisMemoryReclaim
    MemberName: BasisMemoryReclaim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Worlds load and unload additively, and Unity only sweeps unreferenced assets on its own for a\n single (non-additive) LoadScene, so without this nothing on the client ever reclaims what a\n world change orphans.\n \n\nDeliberately NOT driven off `SceneManager.sceneUnloaded`: BasisRuntimeSpawnRegistry\n unloads prop scenes while the player is in the world, and both halves of a pass (a blocking\n collection, then a sweep of every loaded asset) cost far more than a frame. Callers pick moments\n where a stall is already happening. BasisSceneFactory requests one when the last\n BasisScene has gone and the loading screen is coming up."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
