  - TypeFullName: BasisJiggleSimulationLOD
    MemberName: BasisJiggleSimulationLOD
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Distance-based pause of remote avatars' jiggle simulation itself \u2014 distinct from\n BasisJiggleColliderLOD, which only trims the colliders other jiggle chains bounce\n off. A registered jiggle tree pays a Verlet integrate plus a transform read/write every physics\n tick regardless of whether anyone can actually see it move. Past the cutoff distance, a remote's\n GatorDragonGames.JigglePhysics.JiggleRig components are disabled, which unregisters\n their trees from the global simulation via the package's own OnDisable -> RemoveJiggleTreeSegment\n path; re-enabling re-adds them, which reseeds the verlet state from the current animated bone pose\n rather than resuming mid-motion. That reseed-on-return is the deliberate trade for paying zero\n simulation cost on a far/occluded avatar's jiggle bones instead of a reduced-but-nonzero rate. The\n local player is never touched."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
