  - TypeFullName: BasisVerticalSyncModule+VSyncMode
    MemberName: HeadlessFramesPerSend
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Frames the headless loop runs per outgoing avatar send. The transmit accumulator in\n `BasisTransmissionResults.ScheduleTick` can only fire on a frame boundary, so a frame\n period that does not divide the server's send interval spaces sends unevenly \u2014 25 FPS\n (40ms) against the stock 50ms interval sends at 40/40/40/80ms, which reads as jitter even\n though the average rate is a correct 20 Hz. Two frames per send divides the interval\n exactly and leaves a frame of slack for frame-time variance."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
