    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Applies the HDR mode, clamped by the graphics quality level. Also called by\n `SMModuleQualityAndQualitySetURP` when the quality level changes, so this module\n stays the only writer of the HDR fields while still respecting the tier.\n\n \n\nThe colour buffer is the largest render target in the frame and it is allocated\n per eye in stereo, so 64-bit precision is the most expensive bandwidth choice here.\n Very Low drops HDR entirely; Low caps at 32-bit however the dropdown is set."
    Remarks: 
