  - TypeFullName: SMModuleMotionBlurOverrideURP
    MemberName: SMModuleMotionBlurOverrideURP
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: BasisSettingsBase
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Accessibility settings module that takes motion blur away from the world and gives it to the\n player: strength, streak limit, quality and mode, or zero strength to suppress a world that\n forces motion blur on someone it makes ill.\n\n \n\nUnlike the bloom and fog overrides this does not walk the scene's Volumes, because almost\n no world authors a MotionBlur override at all \u2014 there would be nothing to edit.\n Instead the module owns one global Volume at a priority above anything a scene ships, so it\n wins the blend whether or not the world has an opinion. It is created the first time the\n override is switched on and disabled again when it is switched off, which hands the world's own\n authored motion blur straight back untouched."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
