    ParamNames:
    - null
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Always on, every platform, unconditionally \u2014 maintainer call (2026-08-29): \"should be on, no\n exceptions.\" This used to be Android-only, itself gated on a static `SpaceWarpActive` bool\n set once per `BasisOpenXRManagement.StartSDK()` from a single\n `OpenXRRuntime.IsExtensionEnabled(\"XR_FB_space_warp\")` query \u2014 timing-sensitive against the\n OpenXR runtime, so motion vectors (and Android's SpaceWarp reprojection riding on them)\n flickered on/off across sessions. Setting `Camera.depthTextureMode` does not itself make\n URP schedule the per-renderer `MotionVectorRenderPass` \u2014 that pass is scheduled only when\n something declares `ScriptableRenderPassInput.Motion` (Motion Blur's Camera And Objects\n mode, Global Illumination's temporal filter, or XR's own compositor path on Android) \u2014 so this\n flag being always-on elsewhere costs nothing extra by itself; it is the signal those and any\n future/XR-compositor consumer read."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
