  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: OnDestroy
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - ReleaseInstance(false
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 1
    Summary: "`dropFromLayout` deactivates the object before releasing it.\n BasisAddressablePrefabCache.DestroyInstance destroys via\n Object.Destroy, which Unity defers to the end of the frame, so a released\n element otherwise stays an active child and keeps contributing to its parent layout\n group for the rest of this frame \u2014 the layout then lands wrong for exactly one frame\n (visible when a lazy tab replaces its placeholder). Deactivating applies immediately and\n drops it out of that pass. Skipped when the release is already being driven by\n OnDestroy, where changing active state is not valid."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
