  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPanelJoystickBind
    MemberName: BasisPanelJoystickBind
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Hands one panel slider to a thumbstick, so a value can be tuned while looking at what it\n changes instead of at the menu. The bind is taken from the slider's own options window \u2014\n the same hover gesture that offers a reset (BasisPanelResetGesture) \u2014 and the\n hand that opened that window owns the stick: forward raises the value, back lowers it, for\n as long as the bind is held.\n\n \n\n\n The bind is kept on the slider's BasisSettingsBinding{T} rather than the\n control, because the control is destroyed the moment the menu closes \u2014 which is exactly when\n the stick becomes useful. A rebuilt page re-adopts its slider through\n NotifySliderCreated so the handle tracks the stick again when the menu returns.\n \n\n\n\n\n A sweep is treated like a drag: the value moves live but only reaches disk when the stick\n comes back to centre. See ApplyLive and Commit."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
