  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPanelSearch
    MemberName: BasisPanelSearch
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A search field pinned to the top of a panel page that filters the page down to the rows whose\n title, description or tooltip contain what was typed.\n\n \n\nNothing has to be registered. Every control in the menu is a PanelComponent\n carrying a PanelElementDescriptor, so the built hierarchy already holds every\n label the user can read; filtering reads that hierarchy instead of a parallel index, which\n means a page picks up search for free as rows are added to it.\n\n\n\nThe hierarchy is walked once, into a flat pre-order array whose labels are already\n lowercased \u2014 see Prepare. A keystroke is then two linear passes over that array,\n so cost does not scale with how deeply the page nests or how many components a row carries.\n Applying the result is debounced: the string work is cheap, but switching a few hundred rows\n on and off is a uGUI layout pass, and one of those per character is what makes typing drag.\n\n\n\nOnly rows this search hid are ever shown again. A page that keeps a control hidden for\n its own reasons \u2014 one that applies to a single mode, say \u2014 keeps it hidden, and a control the\n page reveals mid-search is filtered like any other on the next Refresh."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
