  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.void+BasisPanelSearchPopup
    MemberName: BasisPanelSearchPopup
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The search palette: a field and a list of matches, opened from a panel's header rather than\n sitting at the top of every page. One field the user asks for, instead of fifteen they have to\n scroll past.\n \n\n\n Driven onto a stock page panel at runtime rather than subclassing BasisMenuPanel:\n the shared Page prefab carries a plain BasisMenuPanel, so asking Addressables to hand back a\n subclass of it finds nothing and the instantiate fails. Same shape as\n BasisPanelMoveHandle \u2014 a behaviour added to the panel it drives.\n \n\n\n\n\n The popup owns the typing loop and nothing else. Whoever opened it supplies a query delegate\n and keeps its own index; when that index grows \u2014 Settings builds the tabs the user never\n opened in the background \u2014 it calls MarkDirty and the list is asked again."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
