  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.BasisTrackingHardware
    MemberName: BasisTrackingHardware
    Kind: Enum
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: byte
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How a device produces its pose. This is a claim about the tracking technology, not about the\n model, because the technology is what decides how noisy the pose is: an IMU that drifts and\n buzzes and a lighthouse tracker that is quiet to a fraction of a millimetre want opposite\n filtering. Each backend stamps its own devices; Unknown is always safe and means\n \"filter this like anything else\".\n\n Order is load-bearing. Values ascend by how much filtering the technology needs, so a body\n group fed by mixed hardware can take the highest and be filtered for its noisiest contributor.\n Unknown sits at 0 so it loses that comparison to any device that actually identified itself."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
