  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisAudioAndVisemeDriver
    MemberName: AnnounceActive
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True while this player's voice is arriving on the announce channel instead of through\n their own spatial AudioSource. Set by BasisAnnounceAudioDriver.\n \n\nBoth of the rules that normally retire a viseme driver describe a announcing\n player wrongly. An announcer sends on `AnnounceVoiceChannel` only, so their spatial\n receiver goes idle and AudioSourceInactive latches even though they are\n mid-sentence; and announce deliberately ignores distance culling, so the viseme distance\n cutoff retires exactly the players announce exists to make audible. Without this flag the\n driver releases and re-acquires its OpenLipSync context every single frame, which\n throws away the buffered audio before inference ever runs."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
