  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.
    MemberName: ShouldReleaseForIdleSource
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether the player has gone quiet long enough to hand their OpenLipSync slot to\n somebody closer. Judged from TrackedAudioSource, which is the player's\n SPATIAL source \u2014 so an announcer, who sends on the announce channel and therefore never\n feeds that source at all, reads as idle while mid-sentence. Releasing then is not\n merely wasteful: `ProcessAudioSamples` immediately asks for the context back, so\n the driver churns a fresh context every frame and the buffered audio is discarded\n before inference ever sees it, which shows up as a mouth that never moves."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
