  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisFootRotationDebug
    MemberName: BasisFootRotationDebug
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Runtime diagnostic for the foot-IK target rotation. The correct foot orientation is the bone-sim\n WORLD foot (OutgoingWorldData) -- it's the animation/standing foot and is valid every frame, independent\n of the FBIK. So this logs, per foot per frame, how far the rendered foot is from that correct foot\n (the bug magnitude), and for each candidate target rotation how far (candidate*offset) lands from the\n correct foot -- i.e. which target, when fed, makes finalFoot = the correct foot. Measure on foot-IK-ON\n frames (stand still). Stop+Dump writes a CSV + a PASS/FAIL summary naming the target to feed."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
