  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisJiggleInteractionEvents
    MemberName: BasisJiggleInteractionEvents
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Grab and touch notifications for jiggle chains, for issue #685 \u2014 avatars, props and world\n objects that want to react when a player handles them.\n\n Strictly opt in. Nothing is detected for an object until something registers a\n listener for it, and when the listener list is empty the per-frame tick returns on a count\n check. Cost is proportional to the objects that asked for events, never to the number of\n jiggle rigs in the instance \u2014 which is what makes it safe in a thousand-player room where\n almost nobody is listening.\n\n Touch is hand proximity, measured with the same palm-to-fingertip grip volume a grab press\n uses (BasisJiggleGrabPicker), so \"touched\" means the same thing as \"close\n enough to grab\" and no simulation state has to be read back out of the Burst jobs.\n\n Events are edge triggered with a dwell, so a hand resting on a chain produces one begin and\n one end rather than a callback every frame."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
