  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ReleaseConnectionRegistrations
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - _deferredDirectMessages.Clear(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drops every scene-data registration and everything still queued for one. Called when a connection ends,\n because a message index means nothing outside the connection that issued it: the server assigns indices\n from a counter that restarts on an empty instance, so the next server hands the same numbers to\n different objects. Anything kept across a disconnect is therefore actively wrong - a stale registration\n points a live index at the wrong subsystem, and a payload nobody claimed on the last server is replayed\n into whoever claims that index on the next one, carrying a player id from a room that no longer exists.\n\n Everything dropped here re-registers itself on the next connection: `BasisNetworkBehaviour` from\n `Start` on the world and prop objects the teardown rebuilds, and the static services from their own\n join hooks. Batch demux is the one exception - it is session-wide policy rather than per connection, so\n it is re-armed here instead of waiting for a `SetEnabled` call that will never come again."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: HandleOwnershipTransfer
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - HandleOwnership(OwnershipTransferMessage
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Replays messages that arrived before their handler existed, in the order they arrived.\n\n This used to walk the list backwards \u2014 safe for removal during iteration, but it delivered newest\n first, which silently reverses the wire order the transport went to the trouble of guaranteeing. For\n anything sent as a sequence that is fatal rather than untidy: an image pickup joining an instance\n received every chunk of a transfer before the spawn header that opens it, so the chunks were dropped\n as belonging to no transfer, the header then raised a card with nothing left to fill it, and the card\n was removed thirty seconds later when the transfer timed out. Handlers registering during a replay is\n also legal, so the list is settled before anything is invoked."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
