  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: Handle
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - header)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Asks the server for a fresh keyframe of `playerId` after a delta had to be\n dropped for lack of a matching baseline. With the v42 adaptive keyframe stretch, periodic\n keyframes can be seconds apart on idle senders \u2014 recovery is request-driven instead."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: "True when unread bytes are left DELIBERATELY \u2014 the frame was dropped for a reason this code\n expects (no receiver yet, no matching baseline, a control frame). The caller passes this to\n Recycle so the \"bytes remaining, is this a parsing bug?\" warning stays meaningful: those drops\n are routine, and at join they are the common case, which is why that warning used to fire\n constantly on this channel. A false return means the frame was consumed to the end, so anything\n left really is a parsing bug."
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
