  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkHandleRemoval
    MemberName: LifecycleBudgetMillisecondsPerFrame
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: Wall-clock ceiling on the lifecycle drain per frame.
    Remarks: "The count above was documented as \"tuned for ~1ms at ~60fps\", but it cannot know what an\n entry costs. A join runs `CreateRemotePlayer`, and its spawn payload path installs the\n loading avatar \u2014 an Instantiate plus a full `RemoteCalibration`, profiled in the field\n at 0.285 ms each. Twenty of those is 5.8 ms, not 1 ms, and a join storm hits the count every\n frame until it drains. A time budget bounds the actual cost the way the count never could;\n leftover entries stay queued and drain on later frames exactly as an over-count did."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
