  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.NetworkedAvatar.BasisNetworkAvatarCompressor
    MemberName: BasisNetworkAvatarCompressor
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Compresses local avatar bone rotations into the RIG-NEUTRAL generic rotation space using\n \"smallest three\" quaternion encoding.\n\n What goes on the wire is each joint's rotation away from its own rest pose, expressed in\n the avatar's ROOT axes rather than in the bone's authored local axes \u2014 see\n Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisGenericBoneRotation for the derivation\n and for why the old local-frame delta could not be replayed on a different rig. Receivers\n rebuild their own rig's local rotations from it with their own rest frames, so the sender\n never has to know or describe the avatar the pose will be played back on.\n\n ExtractBoneDeltas uses a TransformAccessArray to read bone local rotations,\n then a Burst-compiled IJob maps them into generic space and compresses the bitstream in\n a single pass (BasisBoneDeltaAndCompressJob)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
