  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisAudioReceiver
    MemberName: ShoutGain
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Boost for a player in BasisTalkMode.Shout \u2014 the \"louder\" half of shout,\n the wider rolloff being the other. Not a constant: it is\n BasisVoiceAcoustics.ShoutBoost at this listener's distance, so it is 1\n point blank and grows out to BasisShout.Gain. Written by the transmit\n tick on the main thread, consumed on the audio thread, and ramped there like every\n other gain term, so entering or leaving shout does not step the waveform. It also\n raises the SoftLimit ceiling, without which the limiter takes the boost\n straight back off a signal the talker's own AGC already left near full scale."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
