  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.
    MemberName: ApplySpatialTone
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - data
    - channels
    - ConeShelfDb
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Applies the orientation-dependent tone shaping \u2014 talker mouth directivity\n and listener head shadow \u2014 to the already-written output buffer.\n\n Deliberately NOT folded into ApplyGainAndWrite: the viseme\n driver reads this same buffer straight after the receiver writes it, and\n tilting the spectrum before lip-sync sees it would make a talker's mouth\n shapes depend on which way their head is pointing. So the driver calls\n this after `ProcessAudioSamples` instead. The shaper only ever cuts,\n so running it downstream of the soft limiter cannot reintroduce clipping."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
