  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisNetworkReceiver
    MemberName: GetLatestNetworkPose
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - position
    - rotation
    - v1
    - _poseVersion
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Latest network hips position/rotation/scale, updated every time a buffer\n is enqueued. Available before Compute() processes the queue, so\n calibration can immediately pose the freshly spawned avatar instead of\n leaving it at its prefab transform (which caused remote avatars to\n render at scale (1,1,1) until the interp window seeded \u2014 visible as\n \"scale is wrong when a new person joins\").\n Thread-safe via seqlock: writer increments version before/after writes,\n reader retries if version changed or is odd (write in progress)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
