  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: BoneCount
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Ceiling on how far growth will follow a playerId, taken from the cap the server itself\n advertises (Configuration.PeerLimit, pushed on connect and on every admin change).\n \n\nCapacity is proportional to the largest id handed out, and nothing stops a server from\n giving its first joiner 65534 purely to make the client allocate: that is the same 300 MB by\n another route. A fixed ceiling cannot separate that from a real 65535-cap room, and PeerLimit\n defaults to ushort.MaxValue, so any number small enough to be a defence silently costs a\n legitimately large server every player above it. Bounding by the server's own declared limit\n keeps honest rooms exact at any size and still refuses ids a server has said cannot exist.\n The default is permissive, which is the right way to fail: a room only pays for ids that\n actually arrive."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
