  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: SeedScaleState
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - index
    - ((float3*)_outScales.GetUnsafePtr()
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Seeds all scale-tracking state for a player slot to a known-good value.\n Call at calibration time with the latest stashed network scale so the\n first UpdateAllAvatarsJob tick (before SetFrameInputs has seeded the\n real interp window) computes outScale == seed, sees\n HasScaleChange == false, and does NOT overwrite the value the caller\n already wrote directly to animator.transform.localScale.\n\n Without this seed: prev/target scales retain the last writer's value\n (init (1,1,1) or a reused slot's previous player), the first apply tick\n clobbers the correct calibration-time scale, and the avatar flickers at\n (1,1,1) until enough buffers arrive to seed the real interp window.\n\n Completes any in-flight oneEuroJob first: UpdateAllAvatarsJob reads\n _prevScales and writes _outScales/_lastAppliedScales/_HasScaleChange,\n so mutating those arrays mid-flight is a real data race (not just a\n safety-handle complaint). This is a slow path (avatar calibration), so\n the extra Complete() is noise."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
