  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: SeedPoseState
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - index
    - hipsWorldPosition
    - ((float3*)_targetPositions.GetUnsafePtr()
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Seeds all hips-world pose state for a player slot to a known-good pose.\n Call at calibration time with the latest stashed network pose, immediately after\n snapping the avatar's hips onto it, so the first UpdateAllAvatarsJob tick (before\n SetFrameInputs has seeded the real interp window) outputs that same pose instead of\n the slot's zero init.\n\n Without this seed: prev/target positions hold float3.zero on a fresh slot, so the very\n next LateUpdate's bone jobs write the avatar that was just installed to the world\n origin. The receiver needs BOTH a Current and a Next buffer before ComputeData will\n touch the interp window, so a joining player's fallback avatar stands at (0,0,0) until\n its second pose packet lands, then pops into place. The scale channel had the same\n failure mode; see SeedScaleState.\n\n Clears the 1\u20AC seeded flag so the pose filter restarts from this pose rather than\n easing over from the previous occupant's filtered state.\n\n Completes any in-flight oneEuroJob first for the same reason as\n SeedScaleState: these arrays are read and written by jobs it covers."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
