  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.
    MemberName: ShoutBoost
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - distanceSq
    - minDistance
    - maxBoost
    - rolloff)
    ParamDocs:
    - Squared listener-to-mouth distance, as the transmit tick has it.
    - Radius inside which level stops rising, same one DistanceGain uses.
    - Cap, BasisShout.Gain.
    - "Attenuation the AudioSource will apply at this distance, 0..1. The\n boost is clamped to its reciprocal, which is what makes the guarantee hold for the\n gentler rolloff presets (flat, gradual, a hand-drawn user curve) too: those cost the\n talker little or no level with distance, so there is little or nothing to give back."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Level multiplier for a talker in BasisTalkMode.Shout, between 1 and\n `maxBoost`. It gives back most of what DistanceGain took\n away rather than adding a flat broadband boost, so the boost is nothing at all inside\n `minDistance` and largest out where the listener could barely hear\n them. Multiplied by DistanceGain it never exceeds the level of a normal\n talker at `minDistance`: shouting is louder, never louder than\n someone already standing next to you."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
