    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Time-scale compression for the voice catch-up drain: removes one pitch period\n from a decoded frame by overlap-adding the frame onto itself at its strongest\n autocorrelation lag. Periodic (voiced) audio shortens transparently \u2014 the\n waveform stays phase-continuous \u2014 while unvoiced/transient content reports \"no\n confident period\" and is left untouched. Pure math, no Unity dependencies, so\n it is directly unit-testable."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
