  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.
    MemberName: QueuePickupReweld
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - _pickupReweld.Add(pickup
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Rebuilds the owned-object snapshot if the set changed. The snapshot exists so\n TransmitIfDue can register or unregister owned objects without invalidating the\n enumerator; it used to be rebuilt every frame \u2014 a full HashSet walk (which visits free\n slots, so it costs the high-water capacity rather than the live count) plus a List.Add\n per entry \u2014 for a set that only changes when something is picked up, dropped, spawned or\n despawned. Rebuilding on change is behaviourally identical: a mutation from inside the\n transmit loop already only took effect on the following frame, and still does. The count\n comparison is the cheap guard against a mutation that bypassed Register/UnregisterOwned."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
