  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.BasisSyncReductionJob
    MemberName: BasisSyncReductionJob
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IJobParallelFor
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Nearest-observer distance (and, for relevance-culled objects, the in-radius player set) for\n every locally-owned synced object, in one parallel pass.\n\n This used to run per object, inside TransmitIfDue: each object walked\n BasisNetworkPlayers.ReceiversSnapshot calling GetLatestNetworkPose. That made the POSE\n GATHER itself O(objects x players) \u2014 a thousand props each re-reading the same forty\n players \u2014 on top of the distance math. The driver now gathers each player's position once\n and this job does the cross product in Burst.\n\n The recipient set is emitted as a bitmask over player slots rather than a ushort[] per\n object: jobs cannot allocate, and the mask is a fixed small stride the driver expands only\n for the objects that actually cull."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
