  - TypeFullName: BasisJiggleLodJob
    MemberName: BasisJiggleLodJob
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IJobParallelFor
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Burst parallel: the pure-math half of BasisJiggleColliderLOD.ComputeTier and\n BasisJiggleSimulationLOD.ShouldSimulate, run alongside the transmit tick's\n distance/reduce/cap/dampen chain instead of inline in CompleteTick's PostProcess loop.\n Depends on distanceJobHandle (reads distanceSq); the per-receiver \"current\" inputs are\n mirrored from managed objects in the same FillPositions pass that already visits every\n receiver once per tick (see BasisTransmissionResults.ScheduleTick), so this job adds no new\n managed-object reads of its own.\n\n Logic is kept in sync BY HAND with BasisJiggleColliderLOD.ComputeTier /\n BasisJiggleSimulationLOD.ShouldSimulate \u2014 Burst jobs can't call into those directly (mutable\n managed statics aren't job-safe). Threshold fields are copied from the same statics each tick\n (BasisTransmissionResults.ScheduleTick), so the two can't drift out of agreement with the\n settings UI.\n\n Always scheduled, never conditionally skipped: when a feature is disabled, or a receiver has\n nothing jiggle-capable, the corresponding output is just its mirrored current value copied\n back unchanged. PostProcess's own per-feature/per-receiver gates (unchanged from before this\n job existed) decide whether to act on the output, so a \"disabled\" output is always dead data,\n never misapplied \u2014 see the call site."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
