  - TypeFullName: BasisTransmissionResults
    MemberName: MaxAvatarReloadMillisecondsPerTick
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Wall-clock ceiling on what this tick's range-commit reloads are allowed to cost, mirroring\n `BasisAvatarFarLOD.MaxTransitionMillisecondsPerTick`."
    Remarks: "A count alone could not bound the spike: a reload that goes OUT of range installs the\n loading avatar inline \u2014 an Instantiate plus a full remote calibration \u2014 and unlike the\n in-range direction it never reaches Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisAvatarSetupBudget,\n which only gates the tail of `LoadAvatarRemote`. Measured in the field at ~0.4-0.6 ms\n each, so the count of 8 was worth up to ~5 ms of transmit tick on its own. Over-budget\n transitions stay pending (their commit time has already passed) and retry next tick, which\n is the behaviour the count already had."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisTransmissionResults
    MemberName: MaxAudioStartsPerTick
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Max remote voice sources admitted to `StartAudio` per transmit tick, for the same\n reason MaxAvatarReloadsPerTick exists one branch below."
    Remarks: "A start is not a flag write: it pulls a voice object from the pool (or Instantiates the\n prefab once the pool is dry), adds an AudioSource + spatializer, allocates a clip, and\n pushes the whole Steam Audio parameter set \u2014 every one of which mutates the FMOD DSP\n graph. Measured at ~0.15 ms each, with the graph flushes dominating. A join burst or a\n hearing-range slider move crosses dozens of players at once: 22 starts on one tick was\n 3.4 ms of transmit tick, ~2.5 ms of it DSP flushes.\n \n\nOver-budget starts need no pending state of their own \u2014 the\n `HasAudioSource != canHear` mismatch that admitted them is re-evaluated every tick,\n so they simply retry on the next one. Stops are deliberately NOT budgeted: they free\n resources rather than allocate them, and deferring one leaves an out-of-range player\n audible."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
