    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pure math for gaze-foveated VRS. The foveal falloff is angular (eccentricity from\n the gaze direction), not a UV-space circle \u2014 equal UV distances near the edge of a\n wide-FOV projection span fewer degrees, so a UV circle over-coarsens right next to\n the gaze point when looking away from center. Kept free of engine state so the\n projection round-trip is unit-testable."
    Remarks: 
