  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Rendering.BasisVrsMathTests
    MemberName: BasisVrsMathTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pins the angular gaze-foveation math against the field-verified legacy projection.\n\n The VRS compute shader used to compare tile UVs against a UV-space circle around a\n projected gaze point; it now reconstructs each tile's view ray from the projection\n matrix and rates by eccentricity from the gaze direction. The one thing the old path\n had going for it was that its projection convention (GL.GetGPUProjectionMatrix with\n renderIntoTexture=false, no Y flip) was confirmed correct in-headset. These tests\n guarantee the new inverse mapping is the exact algebraic inverse of that same forward\n projection \u2014 including asymmetric VR frusta and a Y-negated (GPU-flipped) matrix \u2014\n so the convention proof carries over.\n\n Matrices are built by hand rather than via Matrix4x4.Perspective/Frustum/TRS so the\n suite exercises only managed math and stays runnable outside the engine."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
