  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisContentNameVersion
    MemberName: BasisContentNameVersion
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reads a version out of a content NAME, for library entries that have no\n BasisBundleDescription.ContentGroupId to group by.\n\n \n\nContentGroupId is authored in the SDK, so nothing built before it exists carries one \u2014\n and that is precisely the content a creator has been re-uploading by hand under names like\n \"My Avatar v2\". Falling back to the name lets those stack into one card the same way a\n grouped upload does, instead of scattering across the library as unrelated entries.\n\n\n\nThis is a heuristic over creator-chosen text, so it is deliberately conservative: it\n only ever strips a version-looking token from the END of a name, and never strips one when\n doing so would leave nothing but punctuation and digits behind."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
