  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.
    MemberName: LoadXR
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Puts the requested loader at the front of the manager's list and leaves the remaining\n loaders behind it instead of removing them. Unity's XRManagerSettings.InitializeLoader\n walks the list and keeps the first loader that initializes, so ordering \u2014 rather than\n trimming \u2014 is what gives a runtime that isn't installed somewhere to hand off to.\n \n\n\n Trimming was also one-way: the removed loaders were never put back while the app ran,\n so a second VR attempt found an empty list, initialized nothing, and dropped to Desktop\n with no explanation. Rewriting the whole list each time undoes any previous attempt.\n \n\n\n Safe against the loader-list mutation race because the isLoading guard\n means no XRManagerSettings.InitializeLoader is enumerating the list here."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: False when this build has no loader matching `Mode`.
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
