    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Calibration.
    MemberName: TrackedFloor_CancelsAnyVerticalShift_EvenOnesBasisCannotSee
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Body.Standard(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Calibrate anywhere\": with body trackers present, the floor comes from the trackers\n themselves (BasisCalibrationMath.TryEstimateFloorFromTrackers), so the eye height \u2014 and with\n it the whole classification frame \u2014 cancels ANY vertical shift, including ones Basis has no\n bookkeeping for (an OVRAS/SteamVR space drag, a stale grounding lift). This sweeps shifts\n with NO compensation term at all and requires identical eye height and identical roles."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Calibration.
    MemberName: TrackedFloor_RefusesToGuessFromTorsoTrackers
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - evidence"
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The tracked floor must refuse to guess from torso trackers: a lone hip puck (or hip+chest)\n sits half a body above the floor, and treating it as feet would halve the measured eye\n height. Feet come in pairs \u2014 fewer than two trackers in the foot band means no estimate."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
