    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A wearer that has already handed its reference back still carries the version string, and\n releases are looked up by that string \u2014 so a second release from it used to spend somebody\n else's reference. Handing the same wearer back twice (an install that released a failed\n build and then destroyed it, an OnDestroy landing behind an explicit release) must not\n retire a version another wearer is still on: that frees the shared mesh under a live\n renderer, which is exactly the null far LOD mesh and is unrecoverable for it."
