    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The same LOD chain, run at the population the client is actually built for. Every job here\n runs once per remote player per tick, so a rule that is merely inefficient at ten players is\n a frame-time problem at two thousand, and a rule that is subtly wrong is wrong two thousand\n times a frame.\n\n These check crowd-scale PROPERTIES rather than per-index expected values: farther players\n never get better detail, a settled crowd reports no changes at all, the visibility budget is\n honoured exactly, and the quickselect behind it still terminates when every player is stood\n on the same spawn point (its worst case, and a completely ordinary thing for a crowd to do)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
