  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Performance.BasisDistanceLodJobTests
    MemberName: BasisDistanceLodJobTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The per-tick distance pass that decides, for every remote player, whether they are heard,\n drawn, and at what mesh and pose detail. Everything downstream that costs frame time hangs\n off these outputs, so a wrong band here is either a visible pop or milliseconds spent on a\n player nobody can see.\n\n Two behaviours are easy to break and invisible in a screenshot: the enter/exit hysteresis\n (without it a player standing on a boundary loads and unloads every tick), and the fact that\n pose LOD bands off AVATAR RANGE while mesh LOD bands off the mesh-LOD slider, so moving one\n slider must not silently move the other's thresholds.\n\n Jobs are driven through Execute directly, the way BasisVisibilityJobTests does, so the tests\n exercise the arithmetic without going through the scheduler."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
