  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Performance.BasisDynamicResolutionPolicyTests
    MemberName: BasisDynamicResolutionPolicyTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The closed loop that trades render resolution for frame time. It is the one graphics control\n that reacts to lag while the player is looking at it, so its failure modes are all visible:\n oscillating between two scales reads as the image breathing, a step that is too large reads\n as a resolution pop, and reacting to a single slow frame drops the whole image because one\n shader compiled.\n\n The guards against that are the settle window, the smoothing, the asymmetric step limits\n (drop fast, recover slowly) and the dead band around the target. Every test here pins one of\n them by feeding GPU times, since none of it is observable from a screenshot."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
