  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Performance.BasisJiggleLodJobTests
    MemberName: BasisJiggleLodJobTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Jiggle is the dominant per-frame cost in a crowded instance, and two independent LOD systems\n trim it by distance: the collider tier other chains bounce off, and whether a remote's rigs\n simulate at all. Both decisions were moved into a Burst job so they run alongside the\n transmit tick instead of inline, and the job's own summary says its math is kept in sync\n BY HAND with BasisJiggleColliderLOD.ComputeTier and\n BasisJiggleSimulationLOD.ShouldSimulate.\n\n Hand-synced duplicates drift. These tests sweep both implementations over the same distances\n and starting states and require identical answers, so a change to one that misses the other\n fails here rather than showing up as jiggle popping on and off in a busy instance."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
