    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The level table behind Performance Mode: which crowd size arms which level, and how a level\n survives the round trip through the settings file it is stored in.\n\n These are the parts that decide, without asking, that a player's instance is now heavy enough\n to start cutting quality. An off-by-one at a threshold means either a 251-player instance\n that never engages the mode, or a quiet instance that quietly turns the player's settings\n down; a broken id round trip means the level silently resets to Off on the next launch."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
