  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Performance.BasisVisibleAvatarCapJobTests
    MemberName: BasisVisibleAvatarCapJobTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The two hard caps that stop a crowded instance from costing whatever the crowd feels like:\n MaxVisibleAvatars and MaxAudioSources. Both take the in-range set the distance pass produced\n and keep only the closest N, using quickselect rather than a full sort because only the\n boundary matters.\n\n The part worth pinning is not the arithmetic but the edges: which entries count toward the\n cap, what \"0\" means for each job (they disagree, deliberately), and the stickiness bonus that\n stops an avatar hovering on the boundary from being loaded and unloaded every tick, which\n costs far more than simply drawing it would have."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
