  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.
    MemberName: PacketSize_IsUnchangedByTheRepresentation
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Packet size must be untouched. Moving to generic space is a pure change of axes and\n preserves rotation angle exactly (see GenericSpace_PreservesRotationAngle),\n so not one bit of budget had to move with it. If these numbers drift, someone\n rebalanced the bit tables on the assumption that the new representation needs more\n range than the old one did \u2014 it does not, and every bandwidth figure the reduction\n system is tuned against would be off.\n\n 163 is the pre-existing High rotation-block size: 15 body/limb slots at 12 bits per\n component plus the toe/finger tail = 1302 bits. (The class doc on\n BasisBoneRotationCompression still says 148, left over from before the v40 10\u219212 bit\n change; the code has been the source of truth since.)"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
