  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisHandPoseGridBakeParityTests
    MemberName: BasisHandPoseGridBakeParityTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The bake sweep was rewritten to stop allocating a BasisPoseData and its ten Quaternion[3]\n arrays per grid cell, to write the finger muscles straight into the HumanPose instead of\n through per-finger float[4] slices, and to gather the thirty finger bones off the Animator\n instead of building a whole BasisTransformMapping. None of that is allowed to move a single\n cell, so the reference sweep below is the ORIGINAL algorithm kept verbatim and the baked\n grid is compared against it bit for bit.\n\n It also pins the finger ORDER. The rewrite replaced the mapping's per-finger arrays with a\n flat HumanBodyBones table, and a table in the wrong order would swap two fingers' cells\n while leaving every other property of the grid intact."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
