  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisHandPoseSamplerTests
    MemberName: BasisHandPoseSamplerTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards BasisHandPoseSampler, the single copy of the curl/splay \u2192 joint rotation\n interpolation that the local finger job and (once the finger block lands) every remote\n reconstruct through.\n\n Determinism is the load-bearing property here, and it is not the same claim as accuracy.\n The remote apply path skips a localRotation write when the composed rotation is bit-identical\n to last frame's, and it names settled fingers as the main beneficiary. A sampler that returns\n an almost-equal quaternion for unchanged input would defeat that and dirty every remote's\n finger subtree every frame \u2014 a frame-time regression with no visual symptom pointing at hands.\n\n Continuity is the other one: a seam at a grid cell boundary is a visible finger pop, and it is\n invisible to any test that only samples at node coordinates."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
