  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisPickupStealKinematicTests
    MemberName: BasisPickupStealKinematicTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Issue #1042: a Rigidbody prop passed from one player to another slid out of the second holder's\n hand. Grabbing a prop you do not own is a steal, and the ownership round-trip lands\n BasisPickupSyncNetworking.ControlState a whole RTT AFTER the local grab already put\n the prop in the hand, so the steal branch has to leave a live hold alone. It used to re-assert the\n authored (dynamic) kinematic state unconditionally, handing the held prop back to gravity while the\n constraint was still driving it. The first grab never showed it: the spawner already owns the prop,\n so no steal is pending and ControlState is never called for it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisPickupWeldFixture
    MemberName: BasisPickupWeldFixture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 1
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Two clients of one held prop, wired the way production wires them: the holder resolves its hand\n frame through the LOCAL branch of BasisHandGrip.TryGetPlayerFrame (the local rig\n driver's mapping) and the observer through the REMOTE branch (that remote's avatar driver\n references), each with its own rig in its own place.\n\n That split is the whole point. The reconstruction is a change of coordinates, so it is exact for\n ANY frame as long as both ends build the same one \u2014 which means a networked hold can only be wrong\n if the two ends disagree, and the two ends can only disagree where they resolve differently. Suites\n that make both ends a BasisRemotePlayer exercise one branch twice and cannot see it.\n\n The real transmit (`OnBeforeTransmit`) and the real receive path (driver schedule \u2192 complete \u2192\n reweld) run; only the input stack and the transport are staged."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
