    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The holder welds the prop to the POST-IK hand (BasisLocalBoneControl.IKWorldData, published at the\n end of FinishSimulate) but the transmit used to measure it against the LIVE bone transform. Those\n are not the same pose during LateUpdate: with the animator graph in GameTime mode\n (BasisLocalRigDriver.EngineDrivenAnimatorEvaluate) the engine rewrites the avatar's bones in\n PreLateUpdate, so when TransmitOwned runs the live bone carries the ANIMATED pose while the prop is\n still sitting on the SOLVED one from the previous frame.\n\n Measuring a grip against a hand the prop is not on ships an offset no observer can undo: wrong\n position AND wrong rotation, on every remote, for every prop, while the holder's own screen is\n perfect. This stages that split directly."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
