    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Announce mode routes a player's voice onto the announce channel and plays it through a separate,\n non-spatialised AudioSource that ignores distance culling. The viseme driver is shared with\n the normal path, and both of the rules that normally retire it \u2014 the viseme distance cutoff\n and \"the tracked AudioSource went idle\" \u2014 misread an announcer as somebody who has stopped\n talking. These lock the exemptions that keep their mouth moving."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
