  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.MediaPipeTiming
    MemberName: MediaPipeTiming
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Webcam tracking arrives far slower than the game renders \u2014 three models share one worker thread, so the\n real rate is often well under the camera's 30 fps \u2014 and the same result is re-applied every frame until\n the next one lands. Filters therefore have to know the difference between the two clocks.\n\n Running a filter at render rate over a held sample is what makes the hands stutter: the signal is a\n staircase, so a one-euro filter reads each new sample as a burst of speed, opens its cutoff and snaps to\n it, then sits still until the next one. Smoothing must run on the SAMPLE clock, and a separate pass on\n the RENDER clock carries the pose between samples."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
