  - TypeFullName: BasisMediaLogDrain
    MemberName: BasisMediaLogDrain
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The engine's free-text diagnostics, taken off the plugin's process-wide\n ring once per frame and fanned out to the Console and to an in-memory\n tail.\n\n It carries what happens before a session handle exists and after it\n closes (a transport refusal, a WHEP negotiation step, the Vulkan probe's\n cause), so it is process-level rather than per-player.\n The ring behind it is one queue for the whole plugin: every player\n pumps this from its own tick and the first through each frame takes the\n whole queue, so three players in a scene still print each line once.\n\n Driving it from the players rather than from a startup hook is\n deliberate. The drain is a P/Invoke, so anything that calls it loads\n `basis_media`; a client whose scene has no media player in it should\n not be mapping the plugin to poll an empty queue. The cost is that\n lines produced with no player anywhere wait in the ring until one\n appears, or age out of it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
