    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: EffectiveBufferDepthMs
    Kind: Property
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "This player's own depth, when the viewer has tuned it away\n from the default; null while it follows DefaultBufferDepthMs.\n\n Per player because one scene can hold both: a source next door, where\n the point is the latency a shallow buffer buys, and one from the far\n side of the world that only plays smoothly with depth behind it. A\n single figure cannot serve those two at once.\n\n Not serialised and never synced: it describes this viewer's route to\n that source, which no other client shares and no world can know.\n Read when a session opens, so ReopenAtPosition is what\n makes a change take effect on one already running."
    Remarks: "Unity cannot serialise a nullable either way, so\n NonSerializedAttribute changes no behaviour. It stops the\n serialisation analyser reporting a field that is skipped on purpose."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
