  - TypeFullName: void
    MemberName: UserDataHandler
    Kind: Event
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Raised for each SEI user_data_unregistered message (H.264 and H.265\n payload type 5) once playback reaches its timestamp, in timestamp\n order (messages with equal timestamps keep their stream order).\n Every UUID arrives, the encoder's own included (x264 stamps its build\n string on keyframes this way), so a consumer filters on the UUID it\n expects. A seek drops whatever was queued from the old position.\n Messages are held until due whether or not anyone is subscribed, so\n a subscriber attaching mid-session receives everything still to come\n and nothing already past."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
