  - TypeFullName: BasisMediaSessionGovernor
    MemberName: BasisMediaSessionGovernor
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Caps how many media players decode at once on this machine.\n\n Props can carry media players, so the number in a world is not the world\n author's to decide: anyone can spawn more, and every open session costs\n this viewer stream bandwidth, memory and decode work whether or not they are\n looking at it. A handful of autoplaying prop players will exhaust a\n standalone headset's link and frame budget on their own.\n\n The nearest few players stay running and the rest go dormant. Dormant means\n the session is closed rather than paused (a paused session still holds its\n buffer, frame pool and decoder), with the URL and playback position\n remembered, so re-activating costs an ordinary join and lands where the\n player would have been.\n\n The cap is the viewer's setting, never the world's, for the same reason the\n decode route is: it describes this machine."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
