  - TypeFullName: BasisMediaTextureRetirement
    MemberName: BasisMediaTextureRetirement
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Holds a retired output RenderTexture past the session that was drawing into\n it, and issues the plugin's collect event for as long as it does.\n\n On Vulkan the plugin builds an image view over Unity's VkImage and cannot\n destroy it at close time, because Unity may still have command buffers in\n flight; `bm_session_close` parks it for a later render event instead.\n Releasing the RenderTexture at the same time would destroy the image while\n that view still exists, so the texture outlives the close. The parked\n objects are destroyed by a render event and a closed session issues none of\n its own, which is why this issues the collect event while it waits.\n\n Textures are held until the events have been issued, so an app that stops\n rendering holds them until it renders again. That is the same bound the\n plugin's own parking has; releasing on a timer instead would destroy the\n very image the wait protects.\n\n Android only. The D3D11 path rebuilds its consumer on registration and has\n no equivalent requirement."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
