    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Feeds one BasisMediaPlayerAudio output AudioSource by mixing\n its channel(s) from the shared PCM splitter on the audio thread via\n OnAudioFilterRead, instead of a streaming AudioClip. A streaming clip\n buffers roughly its own length ahead of the speaker (~0.5 s, and the\n dominant output latency); OnAudioFilterRead runs per DSP block, so latency\n collapses to the DSP buffer (~tens of ms) and is deterministic.\n\n Spatialisation is preserved: this is a filter component on the\n AudioSource's GameObject, so with the source's Spatialize +\n SpatializePostEffects enabled, Unity runs it BEFORE the spatialiser, and\n Steam Audio (HRTF, occlusion, transmission) or Unity 3D then process the\n audio it generates exactly as they would a clip's. The source still plays\n a short silent looping clip to keep its DSP chain active; this overwrites\n that silence each block.\n\n One tap per output. The owning BasisMediaPlayerAudio binds it\n with the splitter, this output's channel taps, and a gain provider; the\n primary tap also reports the mixed block back for the diagnostics metrics\n (consumed samples / peak / RMS)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
