  - TypeFullName: BasisMultiChannelPcmSplitter
    MemberName: BasisMultiChannelPcmSplitter
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Broadcasts a single interleaved-PCM source to several independent readers.\n\n The engine exposes decoded audio as one interleaved float ring\n (IBasisPcmSource) that can only be consumed once. A single\n pump pulls from it and de-interleaves into a short rolling per-channel\n window; every reader then reads that window at its own cursor. Because\n reads don't consume, any number of outputs can draw from the same channel\n (e.g. the centre channel played in two places), and each output mixes the\n channels it wants via a tap matrix (one mono channel, or a stereo\n downmix).\n\n A single lock guards the pump and the window. Unity may invoke the audio\n callbacks on more than one thread, so the lock keeps the shared source\n ring and the window consistent; the critical sections only copy floats."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
