    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Produces `frames` output frames (interleaved,\n `outChannels` wide) for one reader by mixing source\n channels per `taps`, applying\n `gain`. Returns the frames produced; the caller\n zero-fills the rest. Safe on the audio thread.\n\n `sourceStep` is source frames per output frame:\n the tap renders straight into DSP blocks, so both the device rate\n conversion (Quest runs the DSP at 24 kHz against 48 kHz sources,\n which served 1:1 would play at half speed) and the shared-playback rate\n trim happen here. The cursor and its sub-sample remainder live on the\n reader, so changing the step between calls slews the pull without\n resetting the interpolation. Non-unity steps use linear\n interpolation, over a window SetDecimation has already\n band-limited when the step decimates."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
