  - TypeFullName: OpenLipSync.Inference.StreamingSession
    MemberName: StreamingSession
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IDisposable
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Per-player streaming inference state for a cached-TCN viseme model.\n\n The old path re-ran a 150-frame mel window through the whole network on every 10 ms\n hop and then used only the last frame -- roughly 7.5 GMAC/s per player, which is why\n OpenLipSync needed a slot cap at all. A cached model instead carries each dilated\n conv's history in a small ring, so one hop costs exactly one frame of work\n (~91 MMAC/s per player, ~83x less).\n\n Caches are ping-ponged between two IoBindings: binding A reads caches[0] and writes\n caches[1], binding B does the reverse. Alternating them means no buffer is ever\n copied and nothing is allocated per frame."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
