  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.OpenVR.
    MemberName: ThreadedInputUpdate
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "When true the SteamVR action-state update (UpdateActionState + button/axis/skeleton\n reads \u2014 the bulk of the per-frame input cost) runs on a worker thread, kicked from\n SimulateKick in the driver's Update and joined in SimulateJoin\n at the top of LateUpdate, so it overlaps the engine's Update and animation phases.\n OpenVR interfaces are thread-safe, the update path reads main-thread state only via\n SteamVR_Input.CaptureMainThreadState, and no Basis code touches action state between\n kick and join (the eye driver and the device polls both run after the join)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
