  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.
    MemberName: IsUnset
    Kind: Property
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True only for the entirely-zero entry a deserializer hands back for a table that was\n allocated but never authored.\n \n\nDeliberately strict rather than \"cannot move its shape\". Zeroing\n Gain or collapsing the output range is exactly how a creator switches a\n viseme OFF, and that intent has to survive \u2014 rebuilding those on the default hands the\n shape back to the model, which parks the mouth open on whatever the model reports at\n rest. A profile with nothing set at all is the only unambiguous \"absent\"."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
