  - TypeFullName: BasisFarLodPayload
    MemberName: BasisFarLodPayload
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Versioned binary payload describing a distance far avatar for one avatar: a collapsed\n humanoid skeleton snapshot, a quantized low-poly skinned mesh, and pre-compressed\n texture payloads. Generated by the SDK at bundle build time and carried in\n BasisBundleConnector.FarLodBase64, so it is available from a\n connector-only download without loading the AssetBundle.\n\n The payload arrives over the network (inside the bee connector), so parsing is\n defensive: hard caps on every count, and any violation aborts the parse.\n\n Skeleton convention: bones are humanoid bones only, parented to their nearest humanoid\n ancestor. Rest local TRS is composed through any non-humanoid intermediate transforms at\n T-pose, which keeps `restLocalRotation * networkDelta` world-equivalent to the original\n hierarchy (intermediates are static on remotes). Rest rotations double as the TposeLocal\n array for RemoteBoneJobSystem registration."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisFarLodPayload
    MemberName: MinSupportedVersion
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Oldest payload version this build parses. v1/v2 blobs only existed during development\n and their layout drifted WITHOUT version bumps, so they can misparse into plausible\n garbage (observed as a ~7km mouth offset lever); they are refused outright. Any future\n layout change MUST bump CurrentVersion \u2014 the end marker + exact-length\n check in TryParse then turns a writer/reader mismatch into a rejection, never garbage."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
