  - TypeFullName: BasisFarLodVisibilityCuller
    MemberName: BasisFarLodVisibilityCuller
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Exterior-visibility culling for the far LOD: drops triangles that cannot be seen from any\n outside direction (body skin under clothing, jacket linings, inner mouths, inner hair\n cards) BEFORE decimation, so the whole triangle budget goes to surfaces that exist.\n\n Test: from each triangle centroid, a fan of rays across its normal hemisphere tries to\n escape to open space against a collider of the full snapshot. Any escape = visible.\n Deliberately fail-open \u2014 a kept hidden triangle wastes budget, a culled visible one is a\n hole: grazing directions are included (gap visibility, e.g. armpits), and the one-ring of\n neighbors around every visible triangle is kept to seal cull boundaries under cloth hems.\n\n Alpha-cutout occluders (fishnet, mesh fabrics) occlude as solid geometry here, so surfaces\n only visible through texture holes may be culled \u2014 invisible at far LOD ranges."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
