    Summary: "Property ids of every texture slot a shader declares.\n\n \n\nIds rather than names: the caller wants `Material.GetTexture`, and the name\n overload hashes the string on every call while `Shader.GetPropertyName` allocates one\n to begin with. Reflecting over a Poiyomi-class shader is hundreds of properties, so this is\n the difference between a real cost and none."
