    Summary: "Scheduling shell shared by the Avatar, Prop and World validators.\n\n \n\nWhat this replaced. Each validator subscribed to\n EditorApplication.update and re-ran every check it had on every tick \u2014 a full\n hierarchy walk, an AssetDatabase round trip per texture, a mesh index-buffer copy per skinned\n mesh, sixty times a second, for as long as the inspector was open, whether or not anything had\n changed. That is what made the SDK inspectors feel heavy.\n\n\n\nWhat happens now. Checks are declared as groups and a pass runs all of them, but a\n pass only happens when there is a reason for one: the inspector opening, an undo, an import, or\n an actual edit to something in the editor. Idle costs nothing. Bursts of edits \u2014 dragging a\n slider, scrubbing a value \u2014 are coalesced by MinimumSecondsBetweenPasses so the\n worst case is a few passes a second rather than a pass a frame.\n\n\n\nPlay mode. Nothing is authored in play mode and the editor has better things to do,\n so the triggers are dropped entirely and a Validate button takes their place.\n\n\n\nUploads. Builds call RunAllGroups directly. An upload is never allowed\n to read whatever the panels happen to be showing \u2014 it runs the complete suite, every group, on\n the spot."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
