  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarBitPacking
    MemberName: WritePosition
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Hips world position: 3 \xD7 signed int24 millimetres (\xB18388 m, 1 mm steps) at EVERY\n quality, High included.\n\n High used to keep 3 \xD7 float32. Nothing needed that precision \u2014 the position deadband\n is 2 mm, twice the step this gives \u2014 and float32 cost bandwidth twice over. It is\n 3 bytes wider, and, worse, the delta codec compares this field as raw bytes:\n sub-millimetre mantissa churn on a player who is standing still marked it dirty on\n every frame, so every delta carried 12 bytes of position it did not need to. At 1 mm\n steps a still player's position field goes quiet and drops out of the delta entirely.\n It also turns the server's per-tier repack of this field into a plain copy."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
