  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarChannelMap
    MemberName: BasisAvatarChannelMap
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Builds the per-quality channel decomposition of an avatar payload.\n\n Payload geometry (see BasisAvatarBitPacking / BasisBoneRotationCompression):\n   [position      9 B]  3 x signed int24 millimetres, byte-aligned little-endian\n   [rotation    var B]  bit-packed LSB-first: 21 bone slots (2-bit largest index + 3 x BPC\n                        components) then 10 finger channels (curl + splay), then padding\n   [scale         2 B]  posit16\n   [body rot      7 B]  1 B largest index + 3 x uint16\n   [hips delta    5 B]  3 x signed 13-bit + 1 spare bit\n   [hips rot      7 B]  1 B largest index + 3 x uint16\n   [effectors    35 B]  High only: 8-bit mask + 4 x (3 x 12-bit position, 2-bit index, 3 x 10-bit rotation)\n\n Field indices match BasisAvatarDeltaCompression's dirty-mask fields exactly, so\n the mask's meaning is unchanged from the verbatim-copy codec that preceded this."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarDeadband
    MemberName: BasisAvatarDeadband
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Sub-quantization deadband for the local avatar uplink. Byte-identical suppression\n (BasisAvatarIdleSuppression) almost never fires in VR because sensor noise\n crosses quantization steps every frame; these primitives let the sender compare RAW\n (pre-quantization) values against the values of the last frame actually sent and drop the\n frame when every field moved less than a visibility threshold.\n\n Comparing against the last SENT frame (not the previous frame) bounds the standing error to\n the threshold itself: slow drift accumulates until it exceeds the deadband and then sends.\n Thresholds are chosen at or below the wire's own High-quality quantization step, so a\n suppressed change could barely have been expressed on the wire in the first place \u2014 and the\n noise this suppresses is exactly the shimmer receivers otherwise have to low-pass away.\n\n Pure C# so BasisServerTests can cover it; quaternion dots run in double because the\n tightest thresholds (cos of hundredths of a degree) sit inside float epsilon of 1.0."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
