    Summary: "ORs `value`'s low `bitCount` bits into the buffer. The\n destination range must already be zero \u2014 this is the \"write into a cleared region\" form the\n bone/repack encoders use, and it is kept OR-only so a caller cannot silently start relying\n on it to overwrite. Use Replace when the destination may be dirty.\n\n \n\nByte-at-a-time on purpose; see the store-forwarding note on the type."
