  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisResidualCodec
    MemberName: BasisResidualCodec
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bit-level primitives used by the avatar delta codec: a bounds-checked LSB-first bit cursor and\n zig-zag Exponential-Golomb.\n\n \n\nExp-Golomb spends bits in proportion to magnitude \u2014 1 bit for zero, 3 for \xB11, 5 for\n \xB12..3, and two more per octave after that. A pose field that did not move therefore costs a\n single bit instead of its full width, which is what makes per-component granularity affordable:\n the old codec had to spend a whole bone (38 bits at High) when one of its three components\n moved by one step.\n\n\n\nResiduals are never approximated. A previous revision companded them above a small\n linear zone to cap the code length on fast motion. It was removed: the approximation produced\n up to a 180\xB0 single-frame bone error whenever a smallest-three index flipped, and the\n codec already caps code length correctly by falling back to a verbatim field when residual\n coding would be longer. Exactness costs about a byte a frame and removes a whole class of\n artefact."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
