  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compute.IBasisDistanceSolver
    MemberName: IBasisDistanceSolver
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IDisposable
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A backend that can produce the distance cache.\n\n \n\nDeclared here, in the assembly both sides already reference, so the server can hold a\n solver without referencing the assembly that implements one. That indirection is the whole\n point: the GPU backend carries ILGPU, and this assembly is compiled by Unity.\n\n\n\nResults are two bytes per pair at `(sliceIndex * PlayerCount) + j`. The third\n field the cache carries, `CachedIntervalTicks`, is a pure function of the interval byte\n and is recovered by the caller from a 256-entry table \u2014 sending it would triple the bytes\n crossing the bus to carry no information."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
