  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: ImageShareEgressMegabitsPerSecond
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Server egress one sharing player may spend on image replication, in megabits per second.\n\n A shared image is relayed to every player who is not on a direct P2P link, so the server\n forwards it once per recipient: this budget divided by the fan-out is the rate the sharer\n actually uploads at. The client cannot see how much pipe a server has, so before this was\n advertised it assumed a deliberately timid 4 Mb/s and a busy instance took minutes to move\n one picture no matter how fast either end was. Set it to the share of the uplink an image\n transfer may occupy and the sharer will use it.\n\n Sized per sharer, not in total, so several people sharing at once can cost this much each.\n The worst case is this times the number of simultaneous sharers; on a small pipe divide\n accordingly. 0 leaves the client on its own conservative default."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: ImageShareDownloadMegabitsPerSecond
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Rate the server replays cached images to ONE arriving player, in megabits per second.\n\n This is the download side of image sharing, and it is the server's own send \u2014 not something\n a client can be trusted to pace, because the client never asked for it. When somebody joins,\n the cache hands them every image the room already holds so the original sharers do not have\n to send them all again. That replay used to go out in a single synchronous burst: an\n instance sitting near the cache ceiling would push hundreds of megabytes into one peer's\n reliable queue the moment it connected, which is a bad first ten seconds for that player and\n a spike in server memory for everyone.\n\n Sized per arriving player, so several joining at once cost this much each \u2014 the join burst\n after a restart is the case to size for. 0 = unpaced, which restores the old behaviour."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: ImageShareEgressEnforcementPercent
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Headroom the server-side egress backstop allows over\n ImageShareEgressMegabitsPerSecond before it starts dropping, as a percentage.\n\n The advertised budget and the enforced one must not be the same number. A well-behaved\n client paces itself to the advertised figure, but its accounting is not the server's: it\n measures against its own clock, rounds chunks differently, and bursts across a tick\n boundary. Enforcing at exactly the advertised rate would break honest transfers on jitter\n alone, which is far worse than the abuse it is meant to stop.\n\n 150 = drop only once a sender is sustaining half again what it was told it could have, which\n no honest client does and no rate-limited one can hide behind."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: ImagePickupRangeMeters
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Maximum world-space distance, in metres, at which a player is eligible to receive an image\n pickup. Advertised to clients and applied by the sharing client, so it is a bandwidth budget\n rather than an access control - nothing here or on the receiver rejects an out-of-range image.\n\n The server image cache never learns where anybody is. It offers a joiner the spawn header of\n each image it holds - tens of bytes - and that client measures the distance itself and asks for\n the ones it wants, picking up the rest as it walks toward them. 0 is unlimited: every player\n receives every image, which is how it behaved before this setting."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
