  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: LogConnectionHandshake
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Log the per-connection authentication handshake (\"Processing connection from peer N\",\n \"Sending out Writer with size : N\").\n\n \n\nOff by default because it is two lines per joiner on a path that is walked once per\n join, and a mass rejoin walks it for everybody at once \u2014 a 2000-player instance coming back\n after a restart writes four thousand lines that say nothing a reader can act on. The line\n that matters, \"Peer connected: N\", is always logged, as is every rejection, so the default\n still shows who got in and who did not. Turn this on to trace a handshake that is failing\n between those two points."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
