  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: MaxNetworkIdsPerPlayer
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Most distinct network ids one player may register in a session. Every synced object (prop,\n synced transform, image manager) claims one from a shared 65,536-wide space that is only\n reclaimed when the instance empties, so without a per-player ceiling one client can exhaust\n the whole space and lock everyone else out of registering objects. Defaults to half the\n space, which no honest client approaches; raise it only if a single user legitimately spawns\n tens of thousands of networked objects. 0 or negative restores the generous default rather\n than removing the cap."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
