  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: Register
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - name
    - minCores
    - maxCores
    - _leases.Length
    ParamDocs:
    - Subsystem name for diagnostics.
    - Floor below which the subsystem cannot function.
    - Ceiling past which it cannot convert cores into throughput.
    - Resting share, relative to other leases, when nothing is under load.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Cores held back from the pool for threads that are not pools at all.\n\n The tick loop, logic loop and stats thread are one apiece; the receive threads are one\n per bound socket and are the only ones that reliably pin a core, which is exactly why\n adding sockets on a many-weak-core host helps \u2014 it moves drain work onto dedicated\n threads. Those threads exist whether or not the allocator accounts for them, so handing\n their cores out again is how a \"correctly sized\" pool still ends up fighting for CPU.\n\n Capped at half the machine so a large socket count cannot starve the pools it was grown\n to feed."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
