  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: CompressedAvatarBundleChannel
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Server-only outbound channel carrying multiple avatar quality messages\n to a single receiver, compressed into one UDP datagram that fits the peer MTU.\n Wire format (v53):\n   [flags:1][rawLen:2-LE][compressed( group* )]\n   group := [origChannel:1][n:1][msgLen:2-LE] x n [bodies]\n flags: bits 0-2 codec id, bits 3-7 dictionary generation. Byte 0 was a message count\n through v52 that every decoder documented as a hint and none read, so the hybrid codec\n costs no wire bytes. A v52 client would ignore the byte and LZ4-decode a Zstd bundle\n into garbage rather than rejecting it, which is why v53 is a hard version bump.\n Each [origChannel] is the byte-id or ushort-id avatar quality channel the message would\n have been sent on individually (channels 6-13 / 41-48), or DeltaAvatarChannel. One\n channel byte per RUN, not per entry \u2014 the server channel-sorts a receiver's pending\n messages first so the runs are long, but decoding does not depend on that.\n The DeltaAvatarChannel group's bodies are COLUMN-TRANSPOSED (byte j of every body, then\n byte j+1 of every body); no other group is. See BasisAvatarBundleCodec, which is the\n shared reader, and BundleCompressionExperiment for why.\n Compression is hybrid, chosen per bundle by traffic class: delta-only bundles use LZ4\n (LZ4Codec.Encode at LZ4Level.L00_FAST, K4os.Compression.LZ4 1.3.x); bundles carrying a\n keyframe/full quality channel use Zstd against a trained dictionary. Zstd measured\n 16.7-18.1% smaller on keyframes and 2.8-4.5% LARGER on deltas, which is why the split\n exists. See BasisAvatarBundleZstd."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
