  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: BuildPriorityUnreliableChannelMap
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Channels whose unreliable traffic must not be queued behind, or shed alongside, bulk\n avatar state. Indexed by channel number; handed to the transport, which keeps these in a\n separate per-peer queue drained ahead of everything else.\n\n The distinction is whether a newer packet supersedes an older one. An avatar update does:\n the position queued behind it is the same player a moment later, so discarding the stale\n one costs nothing anybody can see, and that is what makes the bulk queue's drop-oldest\n policy correct. Voice is the opposite \u2014 every packet is a distinct slice of audio, so a\n dropped one is a hole in what somebody said and a late one is no better than a lost one.\n Sharing a queue meant voice was shed at the bulk stream's drop rate, which at overload\n removed roughly every second voice packet on the instance.\n\n Only the voice DATA channels belong here. The recipient-list channels are control traffic:\n low-rate, and their newest message genuinely does supersede the last, so they are bulk."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
