  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Server.Generic.BasisNetworkImageCache
    MemberName: BasisNetworkImageCache
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Keeps the bytes of every shared image in server RAM so the rest of the room can be given a\n picture the sharer only sent to the players standing near it, instead of the sharer having to\n send it again to every arrival.\n\n The cache is deliberately dumb about what an image *is*: it retains the client's own scene\n payloads verbatim and replays them stamped with the original owner's player id. A receiving\n client therefore sees exactly the OpSpawn/OpChunk stream it would have got from the owner,\n and needs no knowledge that the server answered instead.\n\n What it hands a player first is an offer - the sharer's own spawn header, opcode swapped - and\n nothing moves until that client measures the distance for itself and asks. The one thing the\n cache does read out of a payload is where a picture has got to: a spawn header records where a\n picture was hung, and pictures get carried around, so the pose the room last saw is kept and\n written over the header's before an offer or a replay goes out. Anything else about an image\n stays opaque bytes.\n\n Lifetime matches what clients already do with images, so the cache can never show a joiner\n something the room cannot see: an entry is dropped on despawn and when its owner disconnects."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
