  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.BitReader
    MemberName: BitReader
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Rescales one quantized value from `bSrc` bits to `bDst`\n bits, rounding to nearest.\n\n \n\nEvery 3-DOF bone repacks three components into three lower tiers and every finger\n two channels into three, so one avatar frame runs this ~250 times \u2014 and it used to end in\n a 64-bit hardware divide, which is the slowest integer instruction on x86 by a wide margin\n (tens of cycles, and not pipelined, so they cannot overlap). The divisor is\n `2^bSrc - 1`: it depends only on the layout, never on the data, so it is known before\n any player connects and the divide can be a multiply by a fixed reciprocal instead.\n\n\n\nExact by exhaustive check, not by argument.QuantRescaleTable\n verifies each reciprocal against the real division across the divisor's ENTIRE input\n domain at static init, and refuses to install one that disagrees anywhere. A pair that\n fails falls back to a 32-bit divide \u2014 still cheaper than the 64-bit one this replaced,\n because the operands provably fit (see the bound in the table)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.BasisComputeBackend
    MemberName: BasisComputeBackend
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Finds the optional compute backend and hands back a solver, or nothing.\n\n \n\nResolved by name rather than referenced, for the same reason the first-boot tuner\n runs as a child process. The backend carries ILGPU; this assembly has an asmdef and is\n compiled by Unity, where that dependency would have to be vendored as a managed DLL and\n survive IL2CPP to serve a path the client never takes. Going through\n Assembly.LoadFrom means the type is never named at compile time, so Unity sees\n nothing, and a server on a host with no GPU pays one File.Exists.\n\n\n\nEvery failure here is ordinary rather than exceptional \u2014 no file, no driver, no\n device, a kernel that will not compile \u2014 and every one of them means the same thing to the\n caller, which is that the sweep stays on the CPU."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
