  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.
    MemberName: EnableComputeOffload
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The active roster, ordered by player id.\n\n The order matters for one reason and it is a big one. Both O(N squared) passes walk the roster\n as the inner loop and index each receiver's per-peer table by the sender's ID - so the order\n the roster happens to be in is the order those tables are touched in. Unordered, the distance\n sweep computes eight lanes of SIMD and then scatters them to eight unrelated places in an\n array that is megabytes wide at scale; every write is its own cache line and the vector work\n in front of it is wasted. Sorted, the same writes march forward through the table and the pass\n streams. The sort itself is O(N log N) and only runs when somebody joins or leaves, against\n O(N squared) of work per sweep that it makes sequential.\n\n Nothing downstream depends on any particular order - the send loop rotates its start point,\n the position snapshot is written in this same order, and the device path indexes both by the\n same roster position - so this is free to choose the order that the memory likes."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
