    - null
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Forgets everything one receiver knew about a batch of departed senders.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F BOTH halves of the per-peer table. The generation lives in its own array for cache\n reasons, and it is the field this whole pass exists for: clearing only the record would leave\n the next player given this id facing the previous occupant's high generation, and the send\n loop's new-data gate would reject every frame they ever send until their own counter climbed\n past it. Nothing else in the system would report anything wrong.\n\n Split out of the drain so it can be tested against a receiver the test owns, rather than\n against the shared player table that the tick thread and every other fixture also write."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
