  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.PeerTrackingData
    MemberName: PeerTrackingData
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "What one receiver remembers about one sender. There is one of these per ORDERED PAIR of players,\n so every byte here is paid N times per player and N squared across the instance: at 4000 players\n a 32 byte record is half a gigabyte, and the same record at the protocol's 65535 peer ceiling is\n 137. That is why the fields below are the widths they are, and why the hottest field of all does\n not live here at all - see PlayerState.PeerLastSeenGeneration."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
