  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.PeerTrackingData
    MemberName: LastSentTime
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Stopwatch ticks, truncated to 32 bits, of the last send to this receiver from this sender.\n\n Only ever read as `(uint)now - LastSentTime` and compared against an interval, so unsigned\n wraparound is the arithmetic rather than a hazard: at a 10 MHz Stopwatch the counter wraps\n every ~430 seconds and every interval this is compared against is under a second. A pair that\n really has been idle for longer than a wrap gets a uniformly distributed elapsed value, which\n clears an interval of a few hundred milliseconds with overwhelming probability and re-rolls on\n the next tick if it does not."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
