  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.PeerTrackingData
    MemberName: HasDistanceCache
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether the distance sweep has ever written the two cached fields above for this pair.\n\n It used to be implicit: the tick count was zero until the sweep filled it in, and the send\n loop read a zero as \"no cache yet, use the base interval\". With the tick count derived from\n the interval byte that tell is gone - byte zero is a legitimate encoding for the closest\n pairs - so the distinction is carried explicitly. It costs nothing: the record is four byte\n fields wide either way once the two uints are aligned."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
