  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.PlayerState
    MemberName: PeerLastSeenGeneration
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The sender data generation this receiver last got, split out of PeerTrackingData because it\n is the send loop's FIRST test and rejects most pairs before anything else is read.\n\n The loop walks every sender for every receiver, so that one comparison sets the cache traffic\n of the whole pass. Inside the record a 64 byte line carried 2 pairs at the old width and 5 at\n the new one; as its own array it carries 16, so the gate touches a quarter to an eighth of the\n memory it used to. Nothing else in the pass is read densely enough to be worth splitting out\n after this one - the rest is only reached by pairs that survive the gate.\n\n uint, not long: it counts avatar updates, and at 90 Hz the low 32 bits take a year and a half\n to wrap. Compared with `senderGen <= seen`, both truncated the same way."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
