  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.QuantRescaleTable
    MemberName: QuantRescaleTable
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Fixed reciprocals for the only division the avatar repacker performs, so it can be a multiply.\n\n \n\nRescaling a quantized value from `bSrc` bits to `bDst` bits divides by\n `2^bSrc - 1`. Both widths come from the wire layout, so the divisor is one of a handful of\n compile-time-ish constants and is fixed before any player connects \u2014 but written as\n `num / maxSrc` the JIT cannot see that and emits a hardware divide, the slowest integer\n instruction on x86 and one that does not pipeline. The repacker runs this ~250 times per avatar\n frame across three quality tiers, so those divides serialise a meaningful slice of the\n per-sender path.\n\n\n\nThe operands fit in 32 bits, which is what makes this safe. Every layout width is\n at most 16 bits (13 in the current tables), so\n `num = qSrc*maxDst + maxSrc/2 < 2^16 * 2^16 = 2^32`. The old code computed in 64-bit\n purely because the expression was written that way, paying for a 64-bit divide it never needed.\n Even the fallback here \u2014 a 32-bit divide \u2014 is materially cheaper than what it replaces.\n\n\n\nExactness. With `M = ceil(2^S / d)` and `e = M*d - 2^S`, the identity\n `floor(n*M / 2^S) == floor(n / d)` holds for every `n < N` exactly when\n `(N-1)*e < 2^S` \u2014 the standard reciprocal bound, and the reason the shift is searched\n rather than fixed. A pair whose bound cannot be met at any usable shift installs no reciprocal\n and divides. `QuantRescaleTableTests` re-checks every installed reciprocal against real\n division across the divisor's entire input domain, so the closed form above is proven against\n the values rather than merely asserted."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
