    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True when the user belongs to `group`, directly or through the parent\n chain of a group they are in. Walks the same edges ApplyGroupRecursive_NoLock\n does, so a role check and a node check never disagree about inheritance, and treats a\n user absent from the store as a member of the implicit \"default\" group for the same\n reason BuildEffective_NoLock does.\n\n A membership naming a group with no row still counts: the assignment on the user is the\n fact being asked about, and one can name a group that was never defined \u2014 AddUserToGroup\n does not create it, and hand-edited xml need not either. (Deleting a group is not such a\n path: DeleteGroup scrubs the membership off every user.)"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
