  - TypeFullName: SerializableBasis+ServerReadyBatchMessage
    MemberName: ServerReadyBatchMessage
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A run of ServerReadyMessages delivered as one packet, used for the join fill.\n\n A joining client is told about every player already present. Sending one reliable packet each\n meant 1999 packets at a 2000-player scale \u2014 all queued to a single peer in one tight loop, which\n costs per-packet overhead and stalls that client behind its own backlog. Worse, each avatar blob\n was deflated INDIVIDUALLY, which recovers almost nothing: the redundancy is across players (the\n same CDN host on every URL, and one popular avatar worn by hundreds), not inside a single record.\n Batching first and compressing the batch turns that around \u2014 measured ~24x on the avatar bytes.\n\n Wire: [count:ushort][compressed:1][payloadLength:int][payload]\n where payload is count ServerReadyMessages back to back, optionally raw-Deflate'd. The flag is\n per batch because compression is skipped when it does not pay (small batches inflate)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
