  - TypeFullName: SerializableBasis+ServerReadyBatchMessage
    MemberName: MaxInflatedBytes
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Hard ceiling the RECEIVER enforces on an inflated payload, deliberately larger than\n MaxPayloadBytes. Producers append a whole record and flush once the buffer\n has REACHED the cap, and JoinBroadcast.Flush always takes at least one record however\n large, so a real batch runs one record past it. The headroom covers the biggest record\n the protocol can express \u2014 a 64 KB avatar blob plus a 64 KB additional-data section and\n their framing \u2014 while still refusing a bomb long before it costs anything."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
