  - TypeFullName: SerializableBasis+ContentSharePayload
    MemberName: TryParseLink
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - value
    - '''>'''
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether `value` is one plain web address and nothing else. The server\n runs this before relaying a link and every client runs it again before showing or\n opening one, so a modified client cannot talk anybody past it. Beyond http/https only,\n it refuses the shapes people misread: a name ahead of an @ that looks like the site\n (https://trusted.example@evil.example goes to evil.example), backslashes browsers turn\n into slashes, quotes and angle brackets, invisible formatting characters, numbers\n dressed up as site names, and hosts that are not a plain name or address."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
