  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Settings.BasisSettingsSystem
    MemberName: BeginBatch
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Coalesces the per-write tail of SaveString \u2014 the full-file save, the\n OnSettingsFinishedChanges broadcast and ForceQualityRefresh \u2014\n across a burst of writes, so a caller that changes fifty settings at once pays for that\n tail once instead of fifty times.\n\n \n\nPer-key OnSettingChanged still fires inline, in write order, so every\n module applies its value exactly when it did before. Only the once-per-change tail moves\n to the end of the burst, which is where it always belonged: the save writes the whole\n dictionary anyway, the finished-changes broadcast is a \"push current state\" pass, and\n `SetQualityLevel(level, applyExpensiveChanges: true)` re-uploads every texture mip.\n Running that chain per setting is what made a Performance Mode level change a\n multi-second main-thread stall \u2014 long enough for the XR compositor to drop the app.\n\n\n\nNesting is counted, so a batch inside a batch flushes once at the outermost exit.\n Always pair with EndBatch in a `finally`, or use Batch."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
