    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Write `weights` onto `mesh`, in shape-index order.\n The exact mirror of GetWeights and clamped the same way.\n\n `epsilon` at or below 0 writes every shape unconditionally, which is\n the cheapest thing to do when you know the values changed. Above 0, each shape's\n current weight is read back first and the write is skipped when it would move the\n weight by less than that \u2014 worth it when most shapes are still, since SetBlendShapeWeight\n dirties the skinned mesh and a read does not. If you are mirroring rather than\n computing, prefer the bound instance path, which caches the last value written and gets\n the same skip without the read-back."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: How many shapes were considered.
    Value: 
