  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.
    MemberName: BindMeshes
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - sourceMeshes
    - targetMeshes
    - (disposed
    ParamDocs:
    - "Object whose destruction ends the subscription \u2014 normally the calling behaviour itself\n (`this`). Pass null to opt out, in which case calling Dispose is mandatory."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bind (or re-bind) the mesh pairs the automatic tick mirrors. Pass the FULL paired\n arrays \u2014 meshes with no blendshapes are dropped here, once, rather than being walked\n every frame. Pairing is by index and the shorter length wins; shapes are matched by\n index too, which is exact when the target is a clone of the source (shared Mesh), and\n if the two meshes disagree on shape count the lower count wins.\n\n Weights are synced in full once here, so the target starts correct rather than waiting\n for the first shape to move.\n\n You do not need to bind to use GetWeights, SetWeights or\n CopyWeights \u2014 those are static and take whatever renderer you hand them.\n Binding buys you the automatic per-frame tick, the change cache and the lifetime\n cleanup."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
