  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisPermissionEventShim
    MemberName: BasisPermissionEventShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: CilboxShim
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Tells a sandboxed script when the local player's permissions change \u2014 the moment they are\n granted or lose admin or moderator \u2014 so a staff-only door, badge or control panel does not\n have to poll BasisPermissionsShim.LocalIsAdmin forever to notice.\n\n Declare the callback and opt in once from `Start`:\n ```\n\n void Start() { GetComponent<BasisPermissionEventShim>(); }\n void OnLocalPermissionsChanged( bool isAdmin, bool isModerator ) { }\n \n```\n A no-argument version is accepted too, for scripts that would rather read\n BasisPermissionsShim themselves. Cilbox creates the component on demand, so\n fetching it is the whole opt-in.\n\n The callback also fires **once shortly after opting in**, carrying whatever is already known,\n so a script never has to read the starting value separately and never has to poll. That first\n call is deferred a frame rather than made inside `GetComponent`, so it cannot re-enter a\n script that is still running its own `Start`.\n\n Permissions arrive with the join handshake, and the local set is data the client already\n holds \u2014 this is the same signal the client's own Settings panel uses to decide whether to\n show its Admin tab, so a world and the menu never disagree. Nothing here is a write handle\n and no other player's permissions cross the boundary; that stays behind\n BasisPermissionsShim.IsAdmin, which asks the server.\n\n Callbacks are resolved by name off the script rather than subscribed as a delegate,\n deliberately: an interpreted delegate cannot be unsubscribed, and the underlying event\n outlives any one world script, so handing it one would leak the whole interpreted object.\n\n This type is method-restricted in `CilboxSceneBasis.extraMethodWhitelist`,\n `CilboxAvatarBasis.extraMethodWhitelist` and `CilboxPropBasis.extraMethodWhitelist`."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
