  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisSharedRandomShim
    MemberName: BasisSharedRandomShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Random numbers every client agrees on without sending a message. Value(seed, index) is a pure\n hash, so the same seed and index give the same number on every machine. The Now* helpers use\n the server clock cut into windows of periodSeconds, so all players roll the same value for the\n same window. Clocks differ by a few milliseconds, so two players can briefly disagree right at\n a window edge; pick a period well above that. Not for anything that must resist prediction."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
