  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisVoiceRoutingShim
    MemberName: BasisVoiceRoutingShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Cilbox-facing facade for the consent-gated voice system (issue #911). A world script\n can ask that a player's voice play from a world object, and stop it again.\n\n Security: everything privacy- or exfiltration-sensitive is withheld. Scripts never\n receive PCM, cannot write recordings to disk, and cannot bypass or forge the\n recordee's consent. This facade only asks the trusted BasisVoiceRecording\n to route already-consented audio to a source that FOLLOWS (never parents under) the\n caller's anchor \u2014 so a script cannot reach the AudioSource via the anchor's hierarchy\n and read its samples. Routes are referenced by opaque integer ids, never host objects.\n This type is method-restricted in `CilboxSceneBasis.extraMethodWhitelist`.\n\n This shim adds no PCM/exfiltration surface of its own. It does NOT address the separate,\n pre-existing platform issue that AudioListener/AudioSource PCM-read APIs are whitelisted\n for scene scripts (see the Cilbox audio whitelist) \u2014 that must be closed independently."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
